window.__F=window.__F||{};window.__F["rs-03.html"]="<div class=\"ac-info\"><p class=\"ac-i-main\">شرح الدليل الأصلي بالإنكليزية.</p><p class=\"ac-i-tip\"><b>متى تستعمله:</b> نظام الوسائد: افصل البطارية وانتظر الوقت المحدد بالدليل قبل أي شغل، ولا تقس دوائر الـ Squib إلا بالأجهزة المسموحة.</p><div class=\"ac-chips\"><span class=\"en-chip\">B = كهرباء الجسم: 54</span></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong>كيف تقرأ كود العطل</strong><small>الرقم بعد الشرطة يدل على نوع العطل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"ac-legend\"><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-11</b><span>قصر على الأرضي</span></div><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-12</b><span>قصر على البطارية</span></div><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-13</b><span>دائرة مفتوحة</span></div><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-15</b><span>قصر على البطارية أو دائرة مفتوحة</span></div><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-16</b><span>الفولتية أقل من الحد</span></div><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-17</b><span>الفولتية أعلى من الحد</span></div><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-2A</b><span>مفتاح عالق Stuck</span></div><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-84 / 85</b><span>الإشارة أقل / أعلى من المدى</span></div><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-92</b><span>أداء ضعيف أو تشغيل غير صحيح</span></div><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-00</b><span>عطل عام أو بدون نوع محدد</span></div></div><p class=\"bcm-note\">الحرف الأول: B = كهرباء الجسم · C = الهيكل والحساسات · P = نقل الحركة · U = اتصال الشبكة. نفّذ دائماً الفحص المسبق Pre-Diagnostic قبل خطوات أي كود.</p></div></details></div><input type=\"search\" class=\"ec-search acc-q\" placeholder=\"ابحث: كود العطل أو كلمة من الوصف\" aria-label=\"بحث\"><p class=\"bcm-note acc-cnt\">54 كود عطل. اضغط على الكود لترى شرحه.</p><div class=\"acc-list\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b0052-11 passenger seatbelt buckle sensor circuit short to ground\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B0052-11</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">PASSENGER SEATBELT BUCKLE SENSOR CIRCUIT SHORT TO GROUND</small><small>العطل: قصر على الأرضي</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">When powered, the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) sends a test current across the Passenger Seat Belt Buckle Switch circuits every 100 ms to verify the integrity of the switch and wiring. The front seat belt switches cannot be adjusted or repaired and, if ineffective or damaged, the entire front seat belt buckle-half unit must be replaced. The airbag warning lamp will display in the instrument cluster for this fault.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">With the ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">If the ORC detects the passenger seat belt buckle switch circuits have been shorted to ground for 2.5 seconds. The active code will change to stored after the ORC verifies the seat belt switch sense circuit voltage has returned to normal voltage range for five seconds.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This DTC may inhibit deployment or modify deployment strategy.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>PASSENGER SEAT BELT BUCKLE SWITCH SENSE CIRCUIT SHORTED TO GROUND</li><li>PASSENGER SEAT BELT BUCKLE SWITCH GROUND CIRCUIT SHORTED TO GROUND</li><li>PASSENGER SEAT BELT BUCKLE SWITCH</li><li>OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER (ORC)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM PRE-DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read ORC DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Record the Environmental Data.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using the recorded Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read ORC DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM INTERMITTENT TEST . Probing of the circuit cavities at the ORC Module body harness connectors or vehicle connectors is only to be done with a approved test lead from the test lead 10159-6 or the use of Breakout Box 8443-55 to prevent vehicle wiring harness connector damage during diagnostic procedures.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK PASSENGER SEAT BELT BUCKLE SWITCH CIRCUITS FOR A SHORT TO GROUND</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition off, disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the Passenger Seat Belt Buckle Switch harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          Check connectors - Clean and repair as necessary.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (R58) Passenger Seat Belt Buckle Switch Sense circuit between the appropriate terminals of the Passenger Seat Belt Buckle Switch harness connector and ground.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (R60) Passenger Seat Belt Buckle Switch Ground circuit between the appropriate terminals of the Passenger Seat Belt Buckle Switch harness connector and ground.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance below 10k Ohms on any of these circuits?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (R58) or (R60) Passenger Seat Belt Buckle Switch circuits for a short to ground.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK OPERATION OF THE PASSENGER SEAT BELT BUCKLE SWITCH</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Replace the Passenger Seat Belt Buckle Switch. Refer to BUCKLE, SEAT BELT, REMOVAL .</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Reconnect the vehicle body harness connector to the Passenger Seat Belt Buckle Switch.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Remove any special tools or jumper wires and reconnect all previously disconnected components - except the Battery.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the standard key ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:       Turn the ignition on, then reconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the keyless ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:       Disconnect the 12-volt battery wait two minutes before proceeding, remove the ORC fuses, connect the 12-volt battery, wait two minutes before proceeding. Cycle the ignition to the On position, then reconnect the ORC fuses. Wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Connect the scan tool to the Data Link Connector - use the most current software available.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Use the scan tool and erase the stored codes in all airbag system modules.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>Turn the Ignition OFF, and wait 15 seconds before turning the Ignition ON.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>Wait one minute, and read active DTCs and if there are none present read the stored DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the scan tool display active B0052-11-PASSENGER SEATBELT BUCKLE SENSOR - CIRCUIT SHORT TO GROUND DTC?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:       Turn the ignition off, disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</p><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        If the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) is dropped at any time, it must be replaced. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Replace the ORC in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Repair is complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b0052-12 passenger seatbelt buckle sensor circuit short to battery\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B0052-12</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">PASSENGER SEATBELT BUCKLE SENSOR CIRCUIT SHORT TO BATTERY</small><small>العطل: قصر على البطارية</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">When powered, the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) sends a test current across the Passenger Seat Belt</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Buckle Switch circuits every 100 ms to verify the integrity of the switch and wiring. The front seat belt switches cannot be adjusted or repaired and, if ineffective or damaged, the entire front seat belt buckle-half unit must be replaced. The airbag warning lamp will display in the instrument cluster for this fault.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">With the ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">If the ORC detects the passenger seat belt buckle switch circuits have been shorted to voltage for 2.5 seconds. The active code will change to stored after the ORC verifies the seat belt switch sense circuit voltage has returned to normal voltage range for five seconds. If the ORC detects the passenger seat belt buckle switch circuits have been open for 2.5 seconds. The active code will change to stored after the ORC verifies the passenger seat belt buckle switch sense circuit voltage has returned to normal voltage range for five seconds.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">If the ORC detects a fault in the seat belt buckle switch circuits for 2.5 seconds, the airbag light will be illuminated. The active code will change to stored after the ORC verifies the seat belt switch sense circuit voltage has returned to normal voltage range for five seconds.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>PASSENGER SEAT BELT BUCKLE SWITCH SENSE CIRCUIT SHORTED TO VOLTAGE</li><li>PASSENGER SEAT BELT BUCKLE SWITCH GROUND CIRCUIT SHORTED TO VOLTAGE</li><li>PASSENGER SEAT BELT BUCKLE SWITCH</li><li>OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER (ORC)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM PRE-DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>DETERMINE ACTIVE OR STORED DTC</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Make sure that the battery is fully charged.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           The scan tool, (special tool #8443A, SRS Load Tool), and DVOM are required to perform the following test.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Select ACTIVE or STORED DTC:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">ACTIVE DTC</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:            If DTC is active, disconnect and reconnect the inline Body/Seat</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">connector and note if DTC remains active. DTC remained active?</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">STORED DTC</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM INTERMITTENT TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK PASSENGER SEAT BELT BUCKLE SWITCH SHORT TO VOLTAGE</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:       Turn the ignition off, disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the Passenger Seat Belt Buckle Switch harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Check connectors - Clean and repair as necessary.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the standard key ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition on, then reconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the keyless ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Disconnect the 12-volt battery wait two minutes before proceeding, remove the ORC fuses, connect the 12-volt battery, wait two minutes before proceeding. Cycle the ignition to the On position, then reconnect the ORC fuses. Wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Measure the voltage on the (R58) Passenger Seat Belt Buckle Switch Sense circuit between the appropriate terminal of the Passenger Seat Belt Buckle Switch harness connector and ground.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Measure the voltage on the (R284) Passenger Seat Belt Buckle Switch Ground circuit between the appropriate terminal of the Passenger Seat Belt Buckle Switch harness connector and ground.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Is there a short to voltage on any of these circuits?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition off, disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (R58), (R284) Passenger Seat Belt Buckle Switch circuit for a short to voltage in accordance with the Service Information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK OPERATION OF THE PASSENGER SEAT BELT BUCKLE SWITCH</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:       Turn the ignition off, disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Replace the Passenger Seat Belt Buckle Switch in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to BUCKLE, SEAT BELT, REMOVAL .</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Reconnect the vehicle body harness connector to the Passenger Seat Belt Buckle Switch.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Remove any special tools or jumper wires and reconnect all previously disconnected components - except the Battery.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the standard key ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition on, then reconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">result in possible serious or fatal injury.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the keyless ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Disconnect the 12-volt battery wait two minutes before proceeding, remove the ORC fuses, connect the 12-volt battery, wait two minutes before proceeding. Cycle the ignition to the On position, then reconnect the ORC fuses. Wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Connect the scan tool to the Data Link Connector - use the most current software available.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Use the scan tool and erase the stored DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>Turn the Ignition OFF, and wait 15 seconds before turning the Ignition ON.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>Wait one minute, and read active DTCs and if there are none present read the stored DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the scan tool display active B0052-12-PASSENGER SEATBELT BUCKLE SENSOR - CIRCUIT SHORT TO BATTERY DTC?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition off, disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        If the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) is dropped at any time, it must be replaced. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the ORC in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair is complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b0052-13 passenger seatbelt buckle sensor circuit open\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B0052-13</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">PASSENGER SEATBELT BUCKLE SENSOR CIRCUIT OPEN</small><small>العطل: دائرة مفتوحة</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">When powered, the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) sends a test current across the Passenger Seat Belt Buckle Switch circuits every 100 ms to verify the integrity of the switch and wiring. The front seat belt switches cannot be adjusted or repaired and, if ineffective or damaged, the entire front seat belt buckle-half unit must be replaced. The airbag warning lamp will display in the instrument cluster for this fault.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">With the ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">If the ORC detects the passenger seat belt buckle switch circuits have been open for 2.5 seconds. The active code will change to stored after the ORC verifies the passenger seat belt buckle switch sense circuit voltage has returned to normal voltage range for five seconds.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This DTC may inhibit deployment or modify deployment strategy.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>PASSENGER SEAT BELT BUCKLE SWITCH SENSE CIRCUIT OPEN</li><li>PASSENGER SEAT BELT BUCKLE SWITCH GROUND CIRCUIT OPEN</li><li>PASSENGER SEAT BELT BUCKLE SWITCH</li><li>OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER (ORC)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM PRE-DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read ORC DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Record the Environmental Data.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using the recorded Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read ORC DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM INTERMITTENT TEST . Probing of the circuit cavities at the ORC Module body harness connectors or vehicle connectors is only to be done with a approved test lead from the test lead 10159-6 or the use of Breakout Box 8443-55 to prevent vehicle wiring harness connector damage during diagnostic procedures.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK (R58) PASSENGER SEAT BELT BUCKLE SWITCH SENSE CIRCUIT AND (R60) PASSENGER SEAT BELT BUCKLE SWITCH GROUND CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:      Turn the ignition off, disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the Passenger Seat Belt Buckle Switch harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the ORC harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Check connectors - Clean and repair as necessary.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Connect the test leads to the DVOM.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (R58) Passenger Seat Belt Buckle Switch Sense circuit between the Passenger Seat Belt Buckle Switch harness connector cavity 1 and the ORC module body harness connector cavity C1-10.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (R60) Passenger Seat Belt Buckle Switch Ground circuit between the Driver Seat Belt Buckle Switch harness connector cavity 2 and the ORC module body harness connector cavity C1-12.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance greater than 1.0 Ohms on any of these circuits?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (R58), (R60) Driver Seat Belt Buckle Switch circuits for an open.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>VERIFY OPEN SWITCH</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Replace the Passenger Seat Belt Buckle Switch. Refer to BUCKLE, SEAT BELT, REMOVAL .</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Reconnect the vehicle body harness connector to the Driver Seat Belt Buckle Switch.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Remove any special tools or jumper wires and reconnect all previously disconnected components - except the Battery.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the standard key ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition on, then reconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the keyless ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Disconnect the 12-volt battery wait two minutes before proceeding, remove the ORC fuses, connect the 12-volt battery, wait two minutes before proceeding. Cycle the ignition to the On position, then reconnect the ORC fuses. Wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Connect the scan tool to the Data Link Connector - use the most current software available.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Use the scan tool and erase the stored DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>Turn the Ignition OFF, and wait 15 seconds before turning the Ignition ON.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>Wait one minute, and read active DTCs and if there are none present read the stored DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the scan tool display active B0052-13-PASSENGER SEATBELT BUCKLE SENSOR - CIRCUIT OPEN DTC?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition off, disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        If the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) is dropped at any time, it must be replaced. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the ORC in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair is complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b0052-2b passenger seatbelt buckle sensor wires shorted together\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B0052-2B</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">PASSENGER SEATBELT BUCKLE SENSOR WIRES SHORTED TOGETHER</small><small>العطل: قصر بين الأسلاك</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">When powered, the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) sends a test current across the Passenger Seat Belt Buckle Switch circuits every 100 ms to verify the integrity of the switch and wiring. The front seat belt switches cannot be adjusted or repaired and, if ineffective or damaged, the entire front seat belt buckle-half unit must be replaced. The airbag warning lamp will display in the instrument cluster for this fault.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">With the ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This DTC sets when the ORC detects the Seat Belt Switch Sense circuit is shorted to ground or the seat belt switch become shorted together for more than 2.5 seconds. This DTC transitions from active to stored when the module sees a recovery from the shorted together condition for greater than five seconds.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This DTC may inhibit deployment or modify deployment strategy.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>PASSENGER SEAT BELT BUCKLE SWITCH SENSE CIRCUIT SHORTED TO GROUND</li><li>PASSENGER SEAT BELT BUCKLE SWITCH SENSE CIRCUIT SHORTED TO THE PASSENGER</li><li>SEAT BELT BUCKLE SWITCH RETURN CIRCUIT</li><li>PASSENGER SEAT BELT BUCKLE SWITCH</li><li>OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER (ORC)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM PRE-DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read ORC DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Record the Environmental Data.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using the recorded Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read ORC DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM INTERMITTENT TEST . Probing of the circuit cavities at the ORC Module body harness connectors or vehicle connectors is only to be done with a approved test lead from the test lead 10159-6 or the use of Breakout Box 8443-55 to prevent vehicle wiring harness connector damage</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">during diagnostic procedures.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK (R58) PASSENGER SEAT BELT BUCKLE SWITCH SENSE CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO THE (R60) PASSENGER SEAT BELT BUCKLE SWITCH RETURN CIRCUIT</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:       Turn the ignition off, disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Locate the Passenger Seat Belt Buckle Switch harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Check connectors - Clean and repair as necessary.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Measure the resistance between the (R58) Passenger Seat Belt Buckle Switch Sense circuit and the (R60) Passenger Seat Belt Buckle Switch Return circuit at the appropriate terminals of the Passenger Seat Belt Buckle Switch harenss connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance below 5k Ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           If the short is found in the Seat Harness, do not attempt to repair the Seat Harness. Replace the Seat Harness in accordance with the Service Information.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair or replace the (R58) Passenger Seat Belt Switch Sense circuit for a short to the (R60) Passenger Seat Belt Switch Return circuit in accordance with the Service Information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK OPERATION OF PASSENGER SEAT BELT BUCKLE SWITCH</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Replace the Passenger Seat Belt Buckle Switch. Refer to BUCKLE, SEAT BELT, REMOVAL .</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Reconnect the ORC harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the standard key ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition on, then reconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the keyless ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Disconnect the 12-volt battery wait two minutes before proceeding, remove the ORC fuses, connect the 12-volt battery, wait two minutes before proceeding. Cycle the ignition to the On position, then reconnect the ORC fuses. Wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">fatal injury.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Connect the scan tool to the Data Link Connector - use the most current software available.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Use the scan tool and erase all codes in the ORC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Perform ORC module reset. Access the Miscellaneous Function menu from the ORC ECU Overview screen on the scan tool to perform this operation.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>Wait one minute, and read active codes.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Did the active B0052-2B-PASSENGER SEATBELT BUCKLE SENSOR - WIRES SHORTED TOGETHER DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        If the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) is dropped at any time, it must be replaced. Failure to take the proper precautions can result in accidental airbag deployment. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition off, disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Replace the ORC in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Repair is complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b0052-95 passenger seatbelt buckle sensor incorrect assembly\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B0052-95</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">PASSENGER SEATBELT BUCKLE SENSOR INCORRECT ASSEMBLY</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">When powered, the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) sends a test current to the Seat Belt Buckle sensors. During this test, the sensors discovered are checked for agreement with the pre-programmed configuration of components assigned to the module.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs once during the initialization process.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">With the ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This DTC sets when the ORC detects the presence of a Seat Belt Buckle sensor circuit while the configuration of the module does not reflect a Seat Belt Buckle sensor should be present. Once set, this DTC is latched for the entire power cycle and requires the module to be re-initalized to set code.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This DTC may inhibit deployment or modify deployment strategy.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>UNUSED SEAT BELT BUCKLE SENSOR CIRCUITS SHORTED TO VOLTAGE, SHORTED TO</li><li>GROUND, OR SHORTED TOGETHER</li><li>OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER (ORC)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read ORC DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Record the Environmental Data.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using the recorded Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read ORC DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM INTERMITTENT TEST . Probing of the circuit cavities at the ORC Module body harness connectors or vehicle connectors is only to be done with a approved test lead from the test lead 10159-6 or the use of Breakout Box 8443-55 to prevent vehicle wiring harness connector damage during diagnostic procedures.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK UNUSED SEAT BELT BUCKLE SENSOR CIRCUITS FOR A SHORT TO VOLTAGE, SHORT TO GROUND, OR SHORT TOGETHER</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check any unused Seat Belt Buckle Sensor circuits for possible short to voltage.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Check any unused Seat Belt Buckle Sensor circuits for possible short to ground.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Check any unused Seat Belt Buckle Sensor circuits for possible short together.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are any of the unused Seat Position circuits shorted?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition off disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair any unused Seat Belt Buckle Sensor circuits that are shorted.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM INTERMITTENT TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:        Make sure the part number of the replacement module is the correct part number for the vehicle.</div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:     If the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) is dropped at any time, it must be replaced. Failure to take the proper precautions can result in accidental airbag deployment. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:     Turn the ignition off disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Replace the ORC in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b0052-9a passenger seatbelt buckle sensor component or system operating\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B0052-9A</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">PASSENGER SEATBELT BUCKLE SENSOR COMPONENT OR SYSTEM OPERATING</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">CONDITIONS</p></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">When powered, the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) sends a test current to the Seat Belt Buckle Sensor to verify the integrity of the sensor and wiring. The presence of this code indicates that any two circuits, from two or more sensors, have become shorted or &quot;coupled&quot; together.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The ORC checks the sensor circuits once during the initialization process.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Module detects that two sensor lines from separate circuits are coupled together.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Once set, the DTC is latched for the entire power cycle and requires the module to be re-initialized to transition code from active to stored. This DTC may inhibit deployment or modify deployment strategy.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>2 SENSOR LINES FROM SEPARATE CIRCUITS COUPLED TOGETHER</li><li>OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER (ORC)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM PRE-DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>DETERMINE ACTIVE OR STORED DTC</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:            Make sure the battery is fully charged.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Perform ORC module reset. Access the Miscellaneous Function menu from the ORC ECU Overview screen on the scan tool to perform this operation.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Using the scan tool, read ORC DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active or stored?</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">ORC - ACTIVE DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLE CODE (DTC)</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Go To 2</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">ORC - STORED DTC</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM INTERMITTENT TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK FOR ADDITIONAL ACTIVE SENSOR DTCS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Using the scan tool, read ORC DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are there squib specific DTCs set as active in addition to B0052-9A-PASSENGER SEATBELT BUCKLE SENSOR - COMPONENT OR SYSTEM OPERATING CONDITIONS?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair all other active sensor specific DTCs before repairing B0052-9A-PASSENGER SEATBELT BUCKLE SENSOR - COMPONENT OR SYSTEM OPERATING CONDITIONS.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>USE THE SCAN TOOL TO IDENTIFY THE COUPLED CIRCUITS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Using the scan tool, identify the two or more Sensor circuits that read SET.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are two or more Sensor circuits DTCs set?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the two or more Sensor circuits for a Sensor Circuit Coupling condition.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM INTERMITTENT TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b007e-11 driver seatbelt retractor pretensioner circuit short to ground\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B007E-11</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">DRIVER SEATBELT RETRACTOR PRETENSIONER CIRCUIT SHORT TO GROUND</small><small>العطل: قصر على الأرضي</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">When powered, the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) sends a test current to the squibs to verify the integrity of the squib and wiring. These circuits are maintained in a &quot;floating&quot; configuration at the module (connected to neither power nor ground) as protection against inadvertent deployment.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) monitors the squib circuits for multiple circuit failures. If the controller detects a circuit value that is out of the allowable range, the ORC will set this DTC.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">In the case that this DTC is set, the squib may still deploy in a crash event.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>DRIVER SEAT BELT RETRACTOR PRETENSIONER LINE 2 CIRCUIT SHORTED TO GROUND</li><li>DRIVER SEAT BELT RETRACTOR PRETENSIONER LINE 1 CIRCUIT SHORTED TO GROUND</li><li>DRIVER SEAT BELT RETRACTOR PRETENSIONER</li><li>OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER (ORC)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM PRE-DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read ORC DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Record the Environmental Data.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using the recorded Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read ORC DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM INTERMITTENT TEST . Probing of the circuit cavities at the ORC Module body harness connectors or vehicle connectors is only to be done with a approved test lead from the test lead 10159-6 or the use of Breakout Box 8443-55 to prevent vehicle wiring harness connector damage during diagnostic procedures.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK FOR SHORTED DRIVER SEAT BELT RETRACTOR PRETENSIONER</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:      Turn the ignition off, disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the Driver Seat Belt Retractor Pretensioner harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Maintain a safe distance from all airbags while performing the following steps. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Check the connectors - Clean and repair as necessary.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Connect the (special tool #8443A, SRS Load Tool) and the (special tool #8443-8, Jumper, SRS Load) to the Driver Seat Belt Retractor Pretensioner harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the standard key ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition on, then reconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the keyless ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Disconnect the 12-volt battery wait two minutes before proceeding, remove the ORC fuses, connect the 12-volt battery, wait two minutes before proceeding. Cycle the ignition to the On position, then reconnect the ORC fuses. Wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read the active ORC DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Does the scan tool display: B007E-11-DRIVER SEATBELT RETRACTOR PRETENSIONER - CIRCUIT SHORT TO GROUND?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition off, disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Driver Seat Belt Retractor Pretensioner in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to RETRACTOR, SEAT BELT, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK (R505) DRIVER SEAT BELT RETRACTOR TENSIONER LINE 1 CIRCUIT AND (R503) DRIVER SEAT BELT RETRACTOR TENSIONER LINE 2 CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO GROUND</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition off, disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the (special tool #8443A, SRS Load Tool) and the (special tool #8443-8, Jumper, SRS Load) from the Driver Seat Belt Retractor Pretensioner harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the ORC harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Check the connectors - Clean and repair as necessary.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Connect the test leads to the DVOM.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (R505) Driver Seat Belt Retractor Tensioner Line 1 circuit between</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">ground and the ORC module body harness connector terminal C2-2.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (R503) Driver Seat Belt Retractor Tensioner Line 2 circuit between ground and the ORC module body harness connector terminal C2-1.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance below 5K Ohms on either circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair or replace the Driver Seat Belt Retractor Tensioner circuits with a resistance below 5K Ohms in accordance with the Service Information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        If the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) is dropped at any time, it must be replaced. Failure to take the proper precautions can result in accidental airbag deployment. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the ORC in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>STORED ORC DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, record and erase all DTCs from all Airbag System Modules.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>If any ACTIVE codes are present they must be resolved before diagnosing any stored codes.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition off, disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Using the wiring diagram/schematic as a guide, inspect the wiring and connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Look for chafed, pierced, pinched, or partially broken wires and broken, bent, pushed out, spread, corroded, or contaminated terminals.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>The following additional checks may assist you in identifying a possible intermittent problem.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Reconnect any disconnected components and harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the standard key ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition on, then reconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the keyless ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Disconnect the 12-volt battery wait two minutes before proceeding, remove the ORC fuses, connect the 12-volt battery, wait two minutes before proceeding. Cycle the ignition to the On position, then reconnect the ORC fuses. Wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>With the scan tool monitor active codes as you work through the following steps.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Maintain a safe distance from all airbags while performing the following steps. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">10</span><span>Wiggle the wiring harness and connectors of the related airbag circuit or component.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">11</span><span>If codes are related to the Driver Airbag circuits, rotate the steering wheel from stop to stop.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">12</span><span>If only stored codes return continue the test until the problem area has been isolated.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">13</span><span>In the previous steps you have attempted to recreate the conditions responsible for setting active DTC in question.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Are any ACTIVE DTCs present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Select the appropriate diagnostic procedure from the Table of Contents in this section. Refer to DIAGNOSIS AND TESTING .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">No problem found at this time. Erase all codes before returning vehicle to customer.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b007e-12 driver seatbelt retractor pretensioner circuit short to battery\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B007E-12</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">DRIVER SEATBELT RETRACTOR PRETENSIONER CIRCUIT SHORT TO BATTERY</small><small>العطل: قصر على البطارية</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">When powered, the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) sends a test current to the squibs to verify the integrity of the squib and wiring. These circuits are maintained in a &quot;floating&quot; configuration at the module (connected to neither power nor ground) as protection against inadvertent deployment.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) monitors the squib circuits for multiple circuit failures. If the controller detects a circuit value that is out of the allowable range, the ORC will set this DTC.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">In the case that this DTC is set, the squib may still deploy in a crash event.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>DRIVER SEAT BELT RETRACTOR PRETENSIONER LINE 2 CIRCUIT SHORTED TO VOLTAGE</li><li>DRIVER SEAT BELT RETRACTOR PRETENSIONER LINE 1 CIRCUIT SHORTED TO VOLTAGE</li><li>DRIVER SEAT BELT RETRACTOR PRETENSIONER</li><li>OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER (ORC)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM PRE-DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read ORC DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Record the Environmental Data.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using the recorded Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read ORC DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM INTERMITTENT TEST . Probing of the circuit cavities at the ORC Module body harness connectors or vehicle connectors is only to be done with a approved test lead from the test lead 10159-6 or the use of Breakout Box 8443-55 to prevent vehicle wiring harness connector damage during diagnostic procedures.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK FOR SHORTED DRIVER SEAT BELT RETRACTOR PRETENSIONER</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:      Turn the ignition off, disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the Driver Seat Belt Retractor Pretensioner harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Check the connectors - Clean and repair as necessary.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Connect the (special tool #8443A, SRS Load Tool) and the (special tool #8443-8, Jumper, SRS Load) to the Driver Seat Belt Retractor Pretensioner harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the standard key ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition on, then reconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">result in possible serious or fatal injury.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the keyless ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Disconnect the 12-volt battery wait two minutes before proceeding, remove the ORC fuses, connect the 12-volt battery, wait two minutes before proceeding. Cycle the ignition to the On position, then reconnect the ORC fuses. Wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read the active ORC DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the scan tool display: B007E-12-DRIVER SEATBELT RETRACTOR PRETENSIONER - CIRCUIT SHORT TO BATTERY?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition off, disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Driver Seat Belt Retractor Tensioner in accordance with the Service Information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Refer to RETRACTOR, SEAT BELT, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK (R505) DRIVER SEAT BELT RETRACTOR TENSIONER LINE 1 CIRCUIT AND (R503) DRIVER SEAT BELT RETRACTOR TENSIONER LINE 2 CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO BATTERY</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition off, disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the (special tool #8443A, SRS Load Tool) and the (special tool #8443-8, Jumper, SRS Load) from the Driver Seat Belt Retractor Pretensioner harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the ORC harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Check the connectors - Clean and repair as necessary.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Connect the test leads to the DVOM.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the standard key ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition on, then reconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the keyless ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Disconnect the 12-volt battery wait two minutes before proceeding, remove the ORC fuses, connect the 12-volt battery, wait two minutes before proceeding. Cycle the ignition to the On position, then reconnect the ORC fuses. Wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Measure the voltage of the (R505) Driver Seat Belt Retractor Tensioner Line 1 circuit between the ORC Module body harness connector terminal C2-2 and ground.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Measure the voltage of the (R503) Driver Seat Belt Retractor Tensioner Line 2 circuit between the ORC Module body harness connector terminal C2-1and ground.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Is there any voltage present on either circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair or replace the Driver Seat Belt Retractor Tensioner circuits with voltage present in accordance with the Service Information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">If the vehicle is equipped with the standard key ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</p><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:         Turn the ignition on, then reconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">If the vehicle is equipped with the keyless ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</p><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:         Disconnect the 12-volt battery wait two minutes before proceeding, remove the ORC fuses, connect the 12-volt battery, wait two minutes before proceeding. Cycle the ignition to the On position, then reconnect the ORC fuses. Wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:         Turn the ignition off, disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the ORC in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to RETRACTOR, SEAT BELT, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>STORED ORC DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, record and erase all DTCs from all Airbag System Modules.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>If any ACTIVE codes are present they must be resolved before diagnosing any stored codes.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition off, disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Using the wiring diagram/schematic as a guide, inspect the wiring and connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Look for chafed, pierced, pinched, or partially broken wires and broken, bent, pushed out, spread, corroded, or contaminated terminals.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>The following additional checks may assist you in identifying a possible intermittent problem.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Reconnect any disconnected components and harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the standard key ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition on, then reconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the keyless ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Disconnect the 12-volt battery wait two minutes before proceeding, remove the ORC fuses, connect the 12-volt battery, wait two minutes before proceeding. Cycle the ignition to the On position, then reconnect the ORC fuses. Wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>With the scan tool monitor active codes as you work through the following steps.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Maintain a safe distance from all airbags while performing the following steps. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">10</span><span>Wiggle the wiring harness and connectors of the related airbag circuit or component.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">11</span><span>If codes are related to the Driver Airbag circuits, rotate the steering wheel from stop to stop.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">12</span><span>If only stored codes return continue the test until the problem area has been isolated.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">13</span><span>In the previous steps you have attempted to recreate the conditions responsible for setting active DTC in question.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Are any ACTIVE DTCs present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Select the appropriate diagnostic procedure. Refer to DTC INDEX .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">No problem found at this time. Erase all codes before returning vehicle to customer.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b007e-13 driver seatbelt retractor pretensioner circuit open\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B007E-13</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">DRIVER SEATBELT RETRACTOR PRETENSIONER CIRCUIT OPEN</small><small>العطل: دائرة مفتوحة</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">When powered, the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) sends a test current to the squibs to verify the integrity of the squib and wiring. These circuits are maintained in a &quot;floating&quot; configuration at the module (connected to neither power nor ground) as protection against inadvertent deployment.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) monitors the squib circuits for multiple circuit failures. If the controller detects a circuit value that is out of the allowable range, the ORC will set this DTC.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This DTC may or may not allow the squib to deploy during a crash event.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>DRIVER SEAT BELT RETRACTOR TENSIONER LINE 2 CIRCUIT OPEN</li><li>DRIVER SEAT BELT RETRACTOR TENSIONER LINE 1 CIRCUIT OPEN</li><li>DRIVER SEAT BELT RETRACTOR TENSIONER</li><li>OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER (ORC)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM PRE-DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read ORC DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Record the Environmental Data.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using the recorded Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read ORC DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM INTERMITTENT TEST . Probing of the circuit cavities at the ORC Module body harness connectors or vehicle connectors is only to be done with a approved test lead from the test lead 10159-6 or the use of Breakout Box 8443-55 to prevent vehicle wiring harness connector damage during diagnostic procedures.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK FOR DRIVER SEAT BELT RETRACTOR TENSIONER CIRCUIT OPEN</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:      Turn the ignition off, disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the Driver Seat Belt Retractor Tensioner harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Do not place an intact undeployed airbag face down on a hard surface, the airbag will propel into the air if accidentally deployed. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Check connectors - Clean and repair as necessary.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Connect the (special tool #8443A, SRS Load Tool) and the (special tool #8443-8, Jumper, SRS</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Load) to the Driver Seat Belt Retractor Pretensioner harness connector.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the standard key ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition on, then reconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the keyless ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Disconnect the 12-volt battery wait two minutes before proceeding, remove the ORC fuses, connect the 12-volt battery, wait two minutes before proceeding. Cycle the ignition to the On position, then reconnect the ORC fuses. Wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read the active ORC DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Does the scan tool display: B007E-13-DRIVER SEATBELT RETRACTOR PRETENSIONER - CIRCUIT OPEN?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition off, disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Replace the Driver Seat Belt Retractor Pretensioner in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to RETRACTOR, SEAT BELT, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK (R505) DRIVER SEAT BELT RETRACTOR TENSIONER LINE 1 CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition off, disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the (special tool #8443A, SRS Load Tool) and the (special tool #8443-8, Jumper, SRS Load) from the Driver Seat Belt Retractor Tensioner harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the ORC harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Check connectors - Clean and repair as necessary.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Connect the test leads to the DVOM.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (R505) Driver Seat Belt Retractor Tensioner Line 1 circuit between</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">the Driver Seat Belt Retractor Tensioner connector terminal 2 and the ORC Module body harness connector terminal C2-2.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance below 1.0 Ohm?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair or replace the (R505) Driver Seat Belt Retractor Tensioner Line 1 circuit in accordance with the Service Information. Then Go To</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK (R503) DRIVER SEAT BELT RETRACTOR TENSIONER LINE 2 CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (R503) Driver Seat Belt Retractor Tensioner Line 2 circuit between the Driver Seat Belt Retractor Tensioner connector terminal 1 and the ORC Module body harness connector terminal C2-1.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance below 1.0 Ohm?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        If the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) is dropped at any time, it must be replaced. Failure to take the proper precautions can result in accidental airbag deployment. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the ORC in accordance with Service Information. Refer to MODULE, OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair or replace the (R503) Driver Seat Belt Retractor Tensioner Line 2 circuit for an open in accordance with the Service Information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>STORED ORC DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, record and erase all DTCs from all Airbag System Modules.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>If any ACTIVE codes are present they must be resolved before diagnosing any stored codes.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition off, disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Using the wiring diagram/schematic as a guide, inspect the wiring and connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Look for chafed, pierced, pinched, or partially broken wires and broken, bent, pushed out, spread, corroded, or contaminated terminals.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>The following additional checks may assist you in identifying a possible intermittent problem.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Reconnect any disconnected components and harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the standard key ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition on, then reconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the keyless ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Disconnect the 12-volt battery wait two minutes before proceeding, remove the ORC fuses, connect the 12-volt battery, wait two minutes before proceeding. Cycle the ignition to the On position, then reconnect the ORC fuses. Wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>With the scan tool monitor active codes as you work through the following steps.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Maintain a safe distance from all airbags while performing the following steps. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">10</span><span>Wiggle the wiring harness and connectors of the related airbag circuit or component.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">11</span><span>If codes are related to the Driver Airbag circuits, rotate the steering wheel from stop to stop.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">12</span><span>If only stored codes return continue the test until the problem area has been isolated.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">13</span><span>In the previous steps you have attempted to recreate the conditions responsible for setting active DTC in question.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Are any ACTIVE DTCs present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Select the appropriate diagnostic procedure. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">No problem found at this time. Erase all codes before returning vehicle to customer.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b007e-2b driver seatbelt retractor pretensioner wires shorted together\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B007E-2B</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">DRIVER SEATBELT RETRACTOR PRETENSIONER WIRES SHORTED TOGETHER</small><small>العطل: قصر بين الأسلاك</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">When powered, the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) sends a test current to the squibs to verify the integrity of the squib and wiring. These circuits are maintained in a &quot;floating&quot; configuration at the module (connected to neither power nor ground) as protection against inadvertent deployment.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) monitors the squib circuits for multiple circuit failures. If the controller detects a circuit value that is out of the allowable range, the ORC will set this DTC.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">In the case that this DTC is set, the squib may still deploy in a crash event.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>DRIVER SEAT BELT RETRACTOR TENSIONER LINE 2 CIRCUIT SHORTED TO THE DRIVER</li><li>SEAT BELT RETRACTOR TENSIONER LINE 1 CIRCUIT</li><li>DRIVER SEAT BELT RETRACTOR PRETENSIONER</li><li>OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER (ORC)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM PRE-DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read ORC DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Record the Environmental Data.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using the recorded Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read ORC DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM INTERMITTENT TEST . Probing of the circuit cavities at the ORC Module body harness connectors or vehicle connectors is only to be done with a approved test lead from the test lead 10159-6 or the use of Breakout Box 8443-55 to prevent vehicle wiring harness connector damage during diagnostic procedures.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK FOR SHORTED DRIVER SEAT BELT RETRACTOR PRETENSIONER</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:      Turn the ignition off, disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the Driver Seat Belt Retractor Pretensioner harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Check the connectors - Clean and repair as necessary.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Connect the (special tool #8443A, SRS Load Tool) and the (special tool #8443-8, Jumper, SRS Load) to the Driver Seat Belt Retractor Pretensioner harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the standard key ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition on, then reconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">result in possible serious or fatal injury.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the keyless ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Disconnect the 12-volt battery wait two minutes before proceeding, remove the ORC fuses, connect the 12-volt battery, wait two minutes before proceeding. Cycle the ignition to the On position, then reconnect the ORC fuses. Wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read the active ORC DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the scan tool display: B007E-2B-DRIVER SEATBELT RETRACTOR PRETENSIONER - WIRES SHORTED TOGETHER?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition off, disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Driver Seat Belt Retractor Pretensioner in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to RETRACTOR, SEAT BELT, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK (R505) DRIVER SEAT BELT RETRACTOR PRETENSIONER FOR A SHORT TO (R503) DRIVER SEAT BELT RETRACTOR PRETENSIONER</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:       Turn the ignition off, disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the (special tool #8443A, SRS Load Tool) and the (special tool #8443-8, Jumper, SRS Load) from the Driver Seat Belt Retractor Pretensioner harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the ORC harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Check connectors - Clean and repair as necessary.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Connect the test leads to the DVOM.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Measure the resistance between the (R505) Driver Seat Belt Retractor Tensioner Line 1 circuit and the (R503) Driver Seat Belt Retractor Tensioner Line 2 circuit at the ORC module body harness connector terminals C2-2 and C2-1.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance below 5K Ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair or replace the (R505) Driver Seat Belt Retractor Tensioner Line 1 circuit for a short to the (R503) Driver Seat Belt Retractor Tensioner Line 2 circuit in accordance with the Service Information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        If the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) is dropped at any time, it must be replaced. Failure to take the proper precautions can result in accidental airbag deployment. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the ORC in accordance with Service Information. Refer to MODULE, OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>STORED ORC DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, record and erase all DTCs from all Airbag System Modules.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>If any ACTIVE codes are present they must be resolved before diagnosing any stored codes.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition off, disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Using the wiring diagram/schematic as a guide, inspect the wiring and connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Look for chafed, pierced, pinched, or partially broken wires and broken, bent, pushed out, spread, corroded, or contaminated terminals.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>The following additional checks may assist you in identifying a possible intermittent problem.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the standard key ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition on, then reconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the keyless ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Disconnect the 12-volt battery wait two minutes before proceeding, remove the ORC fuses, connect the 12-volt battery, wait two minutes before proceeding. Cycle the ignition to the On position, then reconnect the ORC fuses. Wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>Reconnect any disconnected components and harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>With the scan tool monitor active codes as you work through the following steps.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Maintain a safe distance from all airbags while performing the following steps. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">10</span><span>Wiggle the wiring harness and connectors of the related airbag circuit or component.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">11</span><span>If codes are related to the Driver Airbag circuits, rotate the steering wheel from stop to stop.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">12</span><span>If only stored codes return continue the test until the problem area has been isolated.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">13</span><span>In the previous steps you have attempted to recreate the conditions responsible for setting active DTC in question.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Are any ACTIVE DTCs present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Select the appropriate diagnostic procedure from the Table of Contents in this section. Refer to DIAGNOSIS AND TESTING .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">No problem found at this time. Erase all codes before returning vehicle to customer.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b007e-95 driver seatbelt retractor pretensioner incorrect assembly\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B007E-95</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">DRIVER SEATBELT RETRACTOR PRETENSIONER INCORRECT ASSEMBLY</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">When powered, the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) sends a test current to the Seatbelt Retractor Pretensioner. During this test, the sensors discovered are checked for agreement with the pre-programmed configuration of components assigned to the module.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs once during the initialization process.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">With the ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This DTC sets when the ORC detects the presence of a Seatbelt Retractor Pretensioner circuit while the configuration of the module does not reflect a Seatbelt Retractor Pretensioner should be present. Once set, this DTC is latched for the entire power cycle and requires the module to be re-initalized to set code.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This DTC may inhibit deployment or modify deployment strategy.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>UNUSED SEATBELT RETRACTOR PRETENSIONER CIRCUITS SHORTED TO VOLTAGE,</li><li>SHORTED TO GROUND, OR SHORTED TOGETHER</li><li>OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER (ORC)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM PRE-DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read ORC DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Record the Environmental Data.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using the recorded Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read ORC DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM INTERMITTENT TEST .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Probing of the circuit cavities at the ORC Module body harness connectors or vehicle connectors is only to be done with a approved test lead from the test lead 10159-6 or the use of Breakout Box 8443-55 to prevent vehicle wiring harness connector damage during diagnostic procedures.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK UNUSED SEATBELT RETRACTOR PRETENSIONER CIRCUITS FOR A SHORT TO VOLTAGE, SHORT TO GROUND, OR SHORT TOGETHER</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check any unused Seatbelt Retractor Pretensioner circuits for possible short to voltage.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Check any unused Seatbelt Retractor Pretensioner circuits for possible short to ground.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Check any unused Seatbelt Retractor Pretensioner circuits for possible short together.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are any of the unused Seatbelt Retractor Pretensioner circuits shorted?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition off disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair any unused Seatbelt Retractor Pretensioner circuits that are shorted.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM INTERMITTENT TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Make sure the part number of the replacement module is the correct part number for the vehicle.</div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        If the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) is dropped at any time, it must be replaced. Failure to take the proper precautions can result in accidental airbag deployment. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition off disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the ORC in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to RETRACTOR, SEAT BELT, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b007e-9a driver seatbelt retractor pretensioner component or system\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B007E-9A</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">DRIVER SEATBELT RETRACTOR PRETENSIONER COMPONENT OR SYSTEM</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">OPERATING CONDITIONS</p></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">When powered, the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) sends a test current to the Seatbelt Retractor Pretensioner Sensor to verify the integrity of the sensor and wiring. The presence of this code indicates that any two circuits, from two or more sensors, have become shorted or &quot;coupled&quot; together.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The ORC checks the squib circuits once during the initialization process.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Module detects that two squib lines from separate circuits are coupled together.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Once set, the DTC is latched for the entire power cycle and requires the module to be re-initialized to transition code from active to stored. This DTC may inhibit deployment or modify deployment strategy.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>2 SQUIB LINES FROM SEPARATE CIRCUITS COUPLED TOGETHER</li><li>OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER (ORC)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM PRE-DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>DETERMINE ACTIVE OR STORED DTC</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Make sure the battery is fully charged.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Perform ORC module reset. Access the Miscellaneous Function menu from the ORC ECU Overview screen on the scan tool to perform this operation.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Using the scan tool, read ORC DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active or stored?</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">ORC - ACTIVE DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLE CODE (DTC)</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">ORC - STORED DTC</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM INTERMITTENT TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK FOR ADDITIONAL ACTIVE SQUIB DTCS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Using the scan tool, read ORC DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are there squib specific DTCs set as active in addition to B007E-9A-DRIVER SEATBELT RETRACTOR PRETENSIONER - COMPONENT OR SYSTEM OPERATING CONDITIONS?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair all other active sensor specific DTCs before repairing B007E-9A-DRIVER SEATBELT RETRACTOR PRETENSIONER - COMPONENT OR SYSTEM OPERATING CONDITIONS.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>USE THE SCAN TOOL TO IDENTIFY THE COUPLED CIRCUITS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Using the scan tool, identify the two or more Sensor circuits that read SET.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are two or more Sensor circuits DTCs set?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the two or more Sensor circuits for a Sensor Circuit Coupling condition.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM INTERMITTENT TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b0070-11 driver seatbelt buckle pretensioner circuit short to ground\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B0070-11</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">DRIVER SEATBELT BUCKLE PRETENSIONER CIRCUIT SHORT TO GROUND</small><small>العطل: قصر على الأرضي</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">When powered, the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) sends a test current to the squibs to verify the integrity of the squib and wiring. These circuits are maintained in a &quot;floating&quot; configuration at the module (connected to neither power nor ground) as protection against inadvertent deployment.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">With the ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This DTC sets when the ORC detects a short to ground on the squib circuit for more than 2.5 seconds. This DTC transitions from active to stored when the module sees a recovery from a short to ground for greater than 2.5 seconds.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This DTC may inhibit deployment or modify deployment strategy.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>DRIVER SEAT BELT ANCHOR TENSIONER LINE 2 CIRCUIT SHORTED TO GROUND</li><li>DRIVER SEAT BELT ANCHOR TENSIONER LINE 1 CIRCUIT SHORTED TO GROUND</li><li>DRIVER SEAT BELT ANCHOR TENSIONER</li><li>OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER (ORC)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM PRE-DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read ORC DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Record the Environmental Data.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using the recorded Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read ORC DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM INTERMITTENT TEST . Probing of the circuit cavities at the ORC Module body harness connectors or vehicle connectors is only to be done with a approved test lead from the test lead 10159-6 or the use of Breakout Box 8443-55 to prevent vehicle wiring harness connector damage during diagnostic procedures.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK FOR SHORTED DRIVER SEAT BELT BUCKLE TENSIONER CIRCUIT</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:       Turn the ignition off, disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the Driver Seat Belt Buckle Tensioner harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Do not place an intact undeployed airbag face down on a hard surface, the airbag will propel into the air if accidentally deployed. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Check the connectors - Clean and repair as necessary.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Connect the (special tool #8443A, SRS Load Tool) and the (special tool #8443-8, Jumper, SRS Load) to the Driver Seat Belt Buckle Tensioner harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the standard key ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition on, then reconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the keyless ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Disconnect the 12-volt battery wait two minutes before proceeding, remove the ORC fuses, connect the 12-volt battery, wait two minutes before proceeding. Cycle the ignition to the On position, then reconnect the ORC fuses. Wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read the active ORC DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the scan tool display: B0070-11-DRIVER SEATBELT BUCKLE PRETENSIONER - CIRCUIT SHORT TO GROUND</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition off, disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Replace the Driver Seat Belt Buckle Tensioner in accordance with the Service Information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Refer to BUCKLE, SEAT BELT, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK (R55) DRIVER SEAT BELT BUCKLE TENSIONER LINE 1 CIRCUIT AND (R53) DRIVER SEAT BELT BUCKLE TENSIONER LINE 2 CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO GROUND</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:       Turn the ignition off, disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the (special tool #8443A, SRS Load Tool) and the (special tool #8443-8, Jumper, SRS Load) from the Driver Seat Belt Buckle Tensioner harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the ORC harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Check the connectors - Clean and repair as necessary.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Connect the test leads to the DVOM.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (R55) Driver Seat Belt Buckle Tensioner Line 1 circuit between ground and the ORC Module body harness connector terminal C2-6.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (R53) Driver Seat Belt Buckle Tensioner Line 2 circuit between ground and the ORC Module body harness connector terminal C2-5.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance below 5K Ohms on either circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair or replace the Driver Seat Belt Buckle Tensioner circuits with a resistance below 5K Ohms in accordance with the Service Information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        If the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) is dropped at any time, it must be replaced. Failure to take the proper precautions can result in accidental airbag deployment. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the ORC in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>STORED ORC DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, record and erase all DTCs from all Airbag System Modules.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>If any ACTIVE codes are present they must be resolved before diagnosing any stored codes.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition off, disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Using the wiring diagram/schematic as a guide, inspect the wiring and connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Look for chafed, pierced, pinched, or partially broken wires and broken, bent, pushed out, spread, corroded, or contaminated terminals.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>The following additional checks may assist you in identifying a possible intermittent problem.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Reconnect any disconnected components and harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the standard key ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition on, then reconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the keyless ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Disconnect the 12-volt battery wait two minutes before proceeding, remove the ORC fuses, connect the 12-volt battery, wait two minutes before proceeding. Cycle the ignition to the On position, then reconnect the ORC fuses. Wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>With the scan tool monitor active codes as you work through the following steps.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Maintain a safe distance from all airbags while performing the following steps. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">10</span><span>Wiggle the wiring harness and connectors of the related airbag circuit or component.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">11</span><span>If codes are related to the Driver Airbag circuits, rotate the steering wheel from stop to stop.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">12</span><span>If only stored codes return continue the test until the problem area has been isolated.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">13</span><span>In the previous steps you have attempted to recreate the conditions responsible for setting active DTC in question.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Are any ACTIVE DTCs present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Select the appropriate diagnostic procedure. Refer to DTC INDEX .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">No problem found at this time. Erase all codes before returning vehicle to customer.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b0070-12 driver seatbelt buckle pretensioner circuit short to battery\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B0070-12</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">DRIVER SEATBELT BUCKLE PRETENSIONER CIRCUIT SHORT TO BATTERY</small><small>العطل: قصر على البطارية</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">When powered, the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) sends a test current to the squibs to verify the integrity of the squib and wiring. These circuits are maintained in a &quot;floating&quot; configuration at the module (connected to neither power nor ground) as protection against inadvertent deployment.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) monitors the squib circuits for multiple circuit failures. If the controller detects a circuit value that is out of the allowable range, the ORC will set this DTC.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">In the case that this DTC is set, the squib may still deploy in a crash event.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>DRIVER SEAT BELT ANCHOR TENSIONER LINE 2 CIRCUIT SHORTED TO VOLTAGE</li><li>DRIVER SEAT BELT ANCHOR TENSIONER LINE 1 CIRCUIT SHORTED TO VOLTAGE</li><li>DRIVER SEAT BELT ANCHOR TENSIONER</li><li>OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER (ORC)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM PRE-DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read ORC DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Record the Environmental Data.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using the recorded Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read ORC DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM INTERMITTENT TEST . Probing of the circuit cavities at the ORC Module body harness connectors or vehicle connectors is only to be done with a approved test lead from the test lead 10159-6 or the use of Breakout Box 8443-55 to prevent vehicle wiring harness connector damage during diagnostic procedures.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK FOR SHORTED DRIVER SEAT BELT BUCKLE TENSIONER</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:      Turn the ignition off, disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the Driver Seat Belt Buckle Tensioner harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Do not place an intact undeployed airbag face down on a hard surface, the airbag will propel into the air if accidentally deployed. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Check the connectors - Clean and repair as necessary.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Connect the (special tool #8443A, SRS Load Tool) and the (special tool #8443-8, Jumper, SRS</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Load) to the Driver Seat Belt Buckle Tensioner harness connector.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the standard key ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition on, then reconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the keyless ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Disconnect the 12-volt battery wait two minutes before proceeding, remove the ORC fuses, connect the 12-volt battery, wait two minutes before proceeding. Cycle the ignition to the On position, then reconnect the ORC fuses. Wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read the active ORC DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the scan tool display: B0070-12-DRIVER SEATBELT BUCKLE PRETENSIONER - CIRCUIT SHORT TO BATTERY?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition off, disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Replace the Driver Seat Belt Buckle Tensioner in accordance with the Service Information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Refer to BUCKLE, SEAT BELT, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the RESTRAINT SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to STANDARD PROCEDURE .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK (R55) DRIVER SEAT BELT BUCKLE TENSIONER DATA CIRCUIT AND (R53) DRIVER SEAT BELT BUCKLE TENSIONER VOLTAGE CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO BATTERY</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:       Turn the ignition off, disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the (special tool #8443A, SRS Load Tool) and the (special tool #8443-8, Jumper, SRS Load) from the Driver Seat Belt Buckle Tensioner harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the ORC harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Check the connectors - Clean and repair as necessary.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Connect the appropriate test leads to the DVOM.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the standard key ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition on, then reconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the keyless ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Disconnect the 12-volt battery wait two minutes before proceeding, remove the ORC fuses, connect the 12-volt battery, wait two minutes before proceeding. Cycle the ignition to the On position, then reconnect the ORC fuses. Wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Measure the voltage of the (R55) Driver Seat Belt Buckle Tensioner Line 1 circuit between the ORC module body harness connector terminal C2-6 and ground.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Measure the voltage of the (R53) Driver Seat Belt Buckle Tensioner Line 2 circuit between the ORC module body harness connector terminal C2-5 and ground.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there any voltage present on either circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair or replace the Driver Seat Belt Buckle Tensioner circuits with voltage present in accordance with the Service Information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINT SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to STANDARD PROCEDURE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        If the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) is dropped at any time, it must be replaced. Failure to take the proper precautions can result in accidental airbag deployment. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition off, disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the ORC in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINT SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to STANDARD PROCEDURE .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>STORED ORC DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, record and erase all DTCs from all Airbag System Modules.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>If any ACTIVE codes are present they must be resolved before diagnosing any stored codes.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition off, disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Using the wiring diagram/schematic as a guide, inspect the wiring and connectors.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Look for chafed, pierced, pinched, or partially broken wires and broken, bent, pushed out, spread, corroded, or contaminated terminals.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>The following additional checks may assist you in identifying a possible intermittent problem.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Reconnect any disconnected components and harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the standard key ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition on, then reconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the keyless ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Disconnect the 12-volt battery wait two minutes before proceeding, remove the ORC fuses, connect the 12-volt battery, wait two minutes before proceeding. Cycle the ignition to the On position, then reconnect the ORC fuses. Wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>With the scan tool monitor active codes as you work through the following steps.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Maintain a safe distance from all airbags while performing the following steps. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>Wiggle the wiring harness and connectors of the related airbag circuit or component.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">10</span><span>If codes are related to the Driver Airbag circuits, rotate the steering wheel from stop to stop.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">11</span><span>If only stored codes return continue the test until the problem area has been isolated.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">12</span><span>In the previous steps you have attempted to recreate the conditions responsible for setting active DTC in question.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Are any ACTIVE DTCs present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Select the appropriate diagnostic procedure. Refer to DTC INDEX .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">No problem found at this time. Erase all codes before returning vehicle to customer.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b0070-13 driver seatbelt buckle pretensioner circuit open\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B0070-13</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">DRIVER SEATBELT BUCKLE PRETENSIONER CIRCUIT OPEN</small><small>العطل: دائرة مفتوحة</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">When powered, the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) sends a test current to the squibs to verify the integrity of the squib and wiring. These circuits are maintained in a &quot;floating&quot; configuration at the module (connected to neither power nor ground) as protection against inadvertent deployment.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) monitors the squib circuits for multiple circuit failures. If the controller detects a circuit value that is out of the allowable range, the ORC will set this DTC.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">In the case that this DTC is set, the squib may still deploy in a crash event.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>DRIVER SEAT BELT ANCHOR TENSIONER LINE 2 CIRCUIT OPEN</li><li>DRIVER SEAT BELT ANCHOR TENSIONER LINE 1 CIRCUIT OPEN</li><li>DRIVER SEAT BELT ANCHOR TENSIONER</li><li>OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER (ORC)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM PRE-DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read ORC DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Record the Environmental Data.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using the recorded Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read ORC DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM INTERMITTENT TEST . Probing of the circuit cavities at the ORC Module body harness connectors or vehicle connectors is only to be done with a approved test lead from the test lead 10159-6 or the use of Breakout Box 8443-55 to prevent vehicle wiring harness connector damage during diagnostic procedures.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK FOR OPEN DRIVER SEAT BELT BUCKLE TENSIONER</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:      Turn the ignition off, disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the Driver Seat Belt Buckle Tensioner harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Do not place an intact undeployed airbag face down on a hard surface, the airbag will propel into the air if accidentally deployed. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Check the connectors - Clean and repair as necessary.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Connect the (special tool #8443A, SRS Load Tool) and the (special tool #8443-8, Jumper, SRS</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Load) to the Driver Seat Belt Buckle Tensioner harness connector.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the standard key ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition on, then reconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the keyless ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Disconnect the 12-volt battery wait two minutes before proceeding, remove the ORC fuses, connect the 12-volt battery, wait two minutes before proceeding. Cycle the ignition to the On position, then reconnect the ORC fuses. Wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read the active ORC DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the scan tool display: B0070-13-DRIVER SEATBELT BUCKLE PRETENSIONER - CIRCUIT OPEN?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition off, disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Replace the Driver Seat Belt Buckle Tensioner in accordance with the Service Information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Refer to BUCKLE, SEAT BELT, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK (R55) DRIVER SEAT BELT BUCKLE TENSIONER DRIVER SEAT BELT TENSIONER LINE 1 CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:       Turn the ignition off, disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the (special tool #8443A, SRS Load Tool) and the (special tool #8443-8, Jumper, SRS Load) from the Driver Seat Belt Buckle Tensioner harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the ORC harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Check the connectors - Clean and repair as necessary.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Connect the test leads to the DVOM.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (R55) Driver Seat Belt Buckle Tensioner Line 1 circuit between the</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Driver Seat Belt Buckle Tensioner connector terminal 2 and the ORC Module body harness connector terminal C2-6.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance below 1.0 Ohm?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair or replace the (R55) Driver Seat Belt Buckle Tensioner Line 1 circuit in accordance with the Service Information. Then Go To</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK (R53) DRIVER SEAT BELT BUCKLE TENSIONER LINE 2 CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (R53) Driver Seat Belt Buckle Tensioner Line 2 circuit between the Driver Seat Belt Buckle Tensioner harness connector terminal 1 and the ORC Module body harness connector terminal C2-5.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance below 1.0 Ohm?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        If the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) is dropped at any time, it must be replaced. Failure to take the proper precautions can result in accidental airbag deployment. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the ORC in accordance with Service Information. Refer to MODULE, OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair or replace the (R53) Driver Seat Belt Buckle Tensioner Line 2 circuit for an open in accordance with the Service Information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>STORED ORC DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, record and erase all DTCs from all Airbag System Modules.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>If any ACTIVE codes are present they must be resolved before diagnosing any stored codes.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition off, disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Using the wiring diagram/schematic as a guide, inspect the wiring and connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Look for chafed, pierced, pinched, or partially broken wires and broken, bent, pushed out, spread, corroded, or contaminated terminals.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>The following additional checks may assist you in identifying a possible intermittent problem.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Reconnect any disconnected components and harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the standard key ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition on, then reconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the keyless ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Disconnect the 12-volt battery wait two minutes before proceeding, remove the ORC fuses, connect the 12-volt battery, wait two minutes before proceeding. Cycle the ignition to the On position, then reconnect the ORC fuses. Wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>With the scan tool monitor active codes as you work through the following steps.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Maintain a safe distance from all airbags while performing the following steps. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">10</span><span>Wiggle the wiring harness and connectors of the related airbag circuit or component.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">11</span><span>If codes are related to the Driver Airbag circuits, rotate the steering wheel from stop to stop.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">12</span><span>If only stored codes return continue the test until the problem area has been isolated.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">13</span><span>In the previous steps you have attempted to recreate the conditions responsible for setting active DTC in question.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Are any ACTIVE DTCs present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Select the appropriate diagnostic procedure. Refer to DTC INDEX .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">No problem found at this time. Erase all codes before returning vehicle to customer.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b0070-2b driver seatbelt buckle pretensioner wires shorted together\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B0070-2B</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">DRIVER SEATBELT BUCKLE PRETENSIONER WIRES SHORTED TOGETHER</small><small>العطل: قصر بين الأسلاك</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">When powered, the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) sends a test current to the squibs to verify the integrity of the squib and wiring. These circuits are maintained in a &quot;floating&quot; configuration at the module (connected to neither power nor ground) as protection against inadvertent deployment.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) monitors the squib circuits for multiple circuit failures. If the controller detects a circuit value that is out of the allowable range, the ORC will set this DTC.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">In the case that this DTC is set, the squib may still deploy in a crash event.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>DRIVER SEAT BELT ANCHOR TENSIONER LINE 2 CIRCUIT SHORTED TO THE DRIVER SEAT</li><li>BELT ANCHOR TENSIONER LINE 1 CIRCUIT</li><li>DRIVER SEAT BELT ANCHOR TENSIONER</li><li>OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER (ORC)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM PRE-DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read ORC DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Record the Environmental Data.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using the recorded Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read ORC DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM INTERMITTENT TEST . Probing of the circuit cavities at the ORC Module body harness connectors or vehicle connectors is only to be done with a approved test lead from the test lead 10159-6 or the use of Breakout Box 8443-55 to prevent vehicle wiring harness connector damage during diagnostic procedures.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK FOR SHORTED DRIVER SEAT BELT BUCKLE TENSIONER</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:      Turn the ignition off, disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the Driver Seat Belt Buckle Tensioner harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Check connectors - Clean and repair as necessary.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Connect the (special tool #8443A, SRS Load Tool) and the (special tool #8443-8, Jumper, SRS Load) and the Driver Seat Belt Buckle Tensioner harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the standard key ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition on, then reconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">result in possible serious or fatal injury.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the keyless ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Disconnect the 12-volt battery wait two minutes before proceeding, remove the ORC fuses, connect the 12-volt battery, wait two minutes before proceeding. Cycle the ignition to the On position, then reconnect the ORC fuses. Wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read the active ORC DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the scan tool display: B0070-2B-DRIVER SEATBELT BUCKLE PRETENSIONER - WIRES SHORTED TOGETHER?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition off, disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Driver Seat Belt Buckle Tensioner in accordance with the Service Information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Refer to BUCKLE, SEAT BELT, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK (R55) DRIVER SEAT BELT BUCKLE TENSIONER LINE 1 CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO THE (R53) DRIVER SEAT BELT BUCKLE TENSIONER LINE 2 CIRCUIT</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:       Turn the ignition off, disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the (special tool #8443A, SRS Load Tool) and the (special tool #8443-8, Jumper, SRS Load) from the Driver Seat Belt Buckle Tensioner harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the ORC harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Check the connectors - Clean and repair as necessary.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Connect the test leads to the DVOM.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Measure the resistance between the (R55) Driver Seat Belt Tensioner Line 1 circuit at the ORC Module body harness terminal C2-6 and the (R53) Driver Seat Belt Tensioner Line 2 circuit at the ORC Module body harness terminal C2-5.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance below 5K Ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair or replace the (R55) Driver Seat Belt Buckle Tensioner Line 1 circuit for a short to the (R53) Driver Seat Belt Buckle Tensioner Line 2 circuit in accordance with the Service Information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        If the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) is dropped at any time, it must be replaced. Failure to take the proper precautions can result in accidental airbag deployment. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the ORC in accordance with Service Information. Refer to MODULE, OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>STORED ORC DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, record and erase all DTCs from all Airbag System Modules.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>If any ACTIVE codes are present they must be resolved before diagnosing any stored codes.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition off, disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Using the wiring diagram/schematic as a guide, inspect the wiring and connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Look for chafed, pierced, pinched, or partially broken wires and broken, bent, pushed out, spread, corroded, or contaminated terminals.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>The following additional checks may assist you in identifying a possible intermittent problem.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Reconnect any disconnected components and harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the standard key ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition on, then reconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the keyless ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Disconnect the 12-volt battery wait two minutes before proceeding, remove the ORC fuses, connect the 12-volt battery, wait two minutes before proceeding. Cycle the ignition to the On position, then reconnect the ORC fuses. Wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>With the scan tool monitor active codes as you work through the following steps.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Maintain a safe distance from all airbags while performing the following steps. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">10</span><span>Wiggle the wiring harness and connectors of the related airbag circuit or component.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">11</span><span>If codes are related to the Driver Airbag circuits, rotate the steering wheel from stop to stop.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">12</span><span>If only stored codes return continue the test until the problem area has been isolated.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">13</span><span>In the previous steps you have attempted to recreate the conditions responsible for setting active DTC in question.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Are any ACTIVE DTCs present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Select the appropriate diagnostic procedure. Refer to DTC INDEX .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">No problem found at this time. Erase all codes before returning vehicle to customer.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b0070-95 driver seatbelt buckle pretensioner incorrect assembly\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B0070-95</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">DRIVER SEATBELT BUCKLE PRETENSIONER INCORRECT ASSEMBLY</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">When powered, the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) sends a test current to the SeatBelt Buckle Pretensioner Sensors. During this test, the sensors discovered are checked for agreement with the pre- programmed configuration of components assigned to the module.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs once during the initialization process.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">With the ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This DTC sets when the ORC detects the presence of a Seatbelt Buckle Pretensioner circuit while the configuration of the module does not reflect a Seatbelt Buckle Pretensioner should be present. Once set, this DTC is latched for the entire power cycle and requires the module to be re-initalized to set code.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This DTC may inhibit deployment or modify deployment strategy.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>UNUSED SEATBELT BUCKLE PRETENSIONER CIRCUITS SHORTED TO VOLTAGE, SHORTED</li><li>TO GROUND, OR SHORTED TOGETHER</li><li>OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER (ORC)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM PRE-DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read ORC DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Record the Environmental Data.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using the recorded Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read ORC DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM INTERMITTENT TEST .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Probing of the circuit cavities at the ORC Module body harness connectors or vehicle connectors is only to be done with a approved test lead from the test lead 10159-6 or the use of Breakout Box 8443-55 to prevent vehicle wiring harness connector damage during diagnostic procedures.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK UNUSED SEATBELT BUCKLE PRETENSIONER SENSOR CIRCUITS FOR A SHORT TO VOLTAGE, SHORT TO GROUND, OR SHORT TOGETHER</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check any unused Seat Belt Buckle Pretensioner Sensor circuits for possible short to voltage.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Check any unused Seat Belt Buckle Pretensioner Sensor circuits for possible short to ground.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Check any unused Seat Belt Buckle Pretensioner Sensor circuits for possible short together.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are any of the unused Seat Belt Buckle Pretensioner circuits shorted?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition off disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair any unused Seat Belt Buckle Pretensioner Sensor circuits that are shorted.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM INTERMITTENT TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Ensure the part number of the replacement module is the correct part number for the vehicle.</div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        If the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) is dropped at any time, it must be replaced. Failure to take the proper precautions can result in accidental airbag deployment. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition off disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the ORC in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b0070-9a driver seatbelt buckle pretensioner component or system\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B0070-9A</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">DRIVER SEATBELT BUCKLE PRETENSIONER COMPONENT OR SYSTEM</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">OPERATING CONDITIONS</p></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">When powered, the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) sends a test current to the SeatBelt Buckle Pretensioners to verify the integrity of the Pretensioner and wiring. The presence of this code indicates that any two circuits, from two or more Pretensioners, have become shorted or &quot;coupled&quot; together.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The ORC checks the squib circuits once during the initialization process.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Module detects that two squib lines from separate circuits are coupled together.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Once set, the DTC is latched for the entire power cycle and requires the module to be re-initialized to transition code from active to stored. This DTC may inhibit deployment or modify deployment strategy.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>2 SQUIB LINES FROM SEPARATE CIRCUITS COUPLED TOGETHER</li><li>OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER (ORC)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM PRE-DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>DETERMINE ACTIVE OR STORED DTC</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Make sure the battery is fully charged.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Perform ORC module reset. Access the Miscellaneous Function menu from the ORC ECU Overview screen on the scan tool to perform this operation.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Using the scan tool, read ORC DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active or stored?</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">ORC - ACTIVE DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLE CODE (DTC)</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">ORC - STORED DTC</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM INTERMITTENT TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK FOR ADDITIONAL ACTIVE SQUIB DTCS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Using the scan tool, read ORC DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are there squib specific DTCs set as active in addition to B0070-9A-DRIVER SEATBELT BUCKLE PRETENSIONER - COMPONENT OR SYSTEM OPERATING CONDITIONS?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair all other active sensor specific DTCs before repairing B0070-9A-DRIVER SEATBELT BUCKLE PRETENSIONER - COMPONENT OR SYSTEM OPERATING CONDITIONS.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>USE THE SCAN TOOL TO IDENTIFY THE COUPLED CIRCUITS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Using the scan tool, identify the two or more sensor circuits that read SET.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are two or more sensor circuits DTCs set?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the two or more sensor circuits for a Sensor Circuit Coupling condition.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM INTERMITTENT TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b0072-11 passenger seatbelt buckle pretensioner circuit short to ground\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B0072-11</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">PASSENGER SEATBELT BUCKLE PRETENSIONER CIRCUIT SHORT TO GROUND</small><small>العطل: قصر على الأرضي</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">When powered, the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) sends a test current to the squibs to verify the integrity of the squib and wiring. These circuits are maintained in a &quot;floating&quot; configuration at the module (connected to neither power nor ground) as protection against inadvertent deployment.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) monitors the squib circuits for multiple circuit failures. If the</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">controller detects a circuit value that is out of the allowable range, the ORC will set this DTC.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">In the case that this DTC is set, the squib may still deploy in a crash event.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>PASSENGER SEAT BELT ANCHOR TENSIONER LINE 1 CIRCUIT SHORTED TO GROUND</li><li>PASSENGER SEAT BELT ANCHOR TENSIONER LINE 2 CIRCUIT SHORTED TO GROUND</li><li>PASSENGER SEAT BELT ANCHOR TENSIONER</li><li>OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER (ORC)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM PRE-DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read ORC DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Record the Environmental Data.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using the recorded Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read ORC DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM INTERMITTENT TEST . Probing of the circuit cavities at the ORC Module body harness connectors or vehicle connectors is only to be done with a approved test lead from the test lead 10159-6 or the use of Breakout Box 8443-55 to prevent vehicle wiring harness connector damage during diagnostic procedures.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK FOR SHORTED PASSENGER SEAT BELT BUCKLE TENSIONER CIRCUIT</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition off disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the Passenger Seat Belt Buckle Tensioner harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:            Check the connectors - Clean and repair as necessary.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Connect the (special tool #8443A, SRS Load Tool) and the (special tool #8443-8, Jumper, SRS Load) to the Passenger Seat Belt Buckle Tensioner harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the standard key ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition on, then reconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the keyless ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Disconnect the 12-volt battery wait two minutes before proceeding, remove the ORC fuses, connect the 12-volt battery, wait two minutes before proceeding. Cycle the ignition to the On position, then reconnect the ORC fuses. Wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read the active ORC DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Does the scan tool display: B0072-11-PASSENGER SEATBELT BUCKLE PRETENSIONER - CIRCUIT SHORT TO GROUND?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Replace the Passenger Seat Belt Buckle Tensioner in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to BUCKLE, SEAT BELT, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK (R56) PASSENGER SEAT BELT BUCKLE TENSIONER LINE 1 CIRCUIT AND (R54) PASSENGER SEAT BELT TENSIONER LINE 2 CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO GROUND</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition off disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the (special tool #8443A, SRS Load Tool) and the (special tool #8443-8, Jumper, SRS Load) from the Passenger Seat Belt Buckle Tensioner harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the ORC harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Check the connectors - Clean and repair as necessary.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Connect the test leads to the DVOM.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (R56) Passenger Seat Belt Buckle Tensioner Line 1 circuit between the ORC Module body harness terminal C2-81 and ground.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (R54) Passenger Seat Belt Buckle Tensioner Line 2 circuit between the ORC Module body harness terminal C2-82 and ground.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Is the resistance below 10K Ohms on either circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Repair the Passenger Seat Belt Buckle Tensioner circuits with a resistance below 10K Ohms for a short to ground.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        If the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) is dropped at any time, it must be replaced. Failure to take the proper precautions can result in accidental airbag deployment. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Replace the ORC in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b0072-12 passenger seatbelt buckle pretensioner circuit short to battery\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B0072-12</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">PASSENGER SEATBELT BUCKLE PRETENSIONER CIRCUIT SHORT TO BATTERY</small><small>العطل: قصر على البطارية</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">When powered, the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) sends a test current to the squibs to verify the integrity of the squib and wiring. These circuits are maintained in a &quot;floating&quot; configuration at the module (connected to neither power nor ground) as protection against inadvertent deployment.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) monitors the squib circuits for multiple circuit failures. If the controller detects a circuit value that is out of the allowable range, the ORC will set this DTC.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">In the case that this DTC is set, the squib may still deploy in a crash event.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>PASSENGER SEAT BELT ANCHOR TENSIONER LINE 1 CIRCUIT SHORTED TO VOLTAGE</li><li>PASSENGER SEAT BELT ANCHOR TENSIONER LINE 2 CIRCUIT SHORTED TO VOLTAGE</li><li>PASSENGER SEAT BELT ANCHOR TENSIONER</li><li>OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER (ORC)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM PRE-DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read ORC DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Record the Environmental Data.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using the recorded Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read ORC DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM INTERMITTENT TEST .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Probing of the circuit cavities at the ORC Module body harness connectors or vehicle connectors is only to be done with a approved test lead from the test lead 10159-6 or the use of Breakout Box 8443-55 to prevent vehicle wiring harness connector damage during diagnostic procedures.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK FOR SHORTED PASSENGER SEAT BELT BUCKLE TENSIONER</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:       Turn the ignition off disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the Passenger Seat Belt Buckle Tensioner harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Check the connectors - Clean and repair as necessary.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Connect the (special tool #8443A, SRS Load Tool) and the (special tool #8443-8, Jumper, SRS Load) to the Passenger Seat Belt Buckle Tensioner harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the standard key ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition on, then reconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the keyless ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Disconnect the 12-volt battery wait two minutes before proceeding, remove the ORC fuses, connect the 12-volt battery, wait two minutes before proceeding. Cycle the ignition to the On position, then reconnect the ORC fuses. Wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read the active ORC DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the scan tool display: B0072-12-PASSENGER SEATBELT BUCKLE PRETENSIONER - CIRCUIT SHORT TO BATTERY?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Replace the Passenger Seat Belt Buckle Tensioner in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to BUCKLE, SEAT BELT, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK (R56) PASSENGER SEAT BELT BUCKLE TENSIONER LINE 1 CIRCUIT AND (R54) PASSENGER SEAT BELT BUCKLE TENSIONER LINE 2 CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO BATTERY</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:      Turn the ignition off disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the (special tool #8443A, SRS Load Tool) and the (special tool #8443-8, Jumper, SRS Load) from the Passenger Seat Belt Buckle Tensioner harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the ORC harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Check the connectors - Clean and repair as necessary.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Connect the test leads to the DVOM.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the standard key ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition on, then reconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the keyless ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Disconnect the 12-volt battery wait two minutes before proceeding, remove the ORC fuses, connect the 12-volt battery, wait two minutes before proceeding. Cycle the ignition to the On position, then reconnect the ORC fuses. Wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Measure the voltage of the (R56) Passenger Seat Belt Buckle Tensioner Line 1 circuit between the ORC Module body harness terminal C2-81 and ground.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Measure the voltage of the (R54) Passenger Seat Belt Buckle Tensioner Line 2 circuit between the ORC Module body harness terminal C2-82 and ground.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Is there any voltage present on either circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Repair the Passenger Seat Belt Buckle Tensioner circuits with voltage present for a short to battery.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">لا · No</p><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition off disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        If the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) is dropped at any time, it must be replaced. Failure to take the proper precautions can result in accidental airbag deployment. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Replace the ORC in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b0072-13 passenger seatbelt buckle pretensioner circuit open\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B0072-13</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">PASSENGER SEATBELT BUCKLE PRETENSIONER CIRCUIT OPEN</small><small>العطل: دائرة مفتوحة</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">When powered, the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) sends a test current to the squibs to verify the integrity of the squib and wiring. These circuits are maintained in a &quot;floating&quot; configuration at the module (connected to neither power nor ground) as protection against inadvertent deployment.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) monitors the squib circuits for multiple circuit failures. If the controller detects a circuit value that is out of the allowable range, the ORC will set this DTC.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">In the case that this DTC is set, the squib may still deploy in a crash event.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>PASSENGER SEAT BELT ANCHOR TENSIONER LINE 1 CIRCUIT OPEN</li><li>PASSENGER SEAT BELT ANCHOR TENSIONER LINE 2 CIRCUIT OPEN</li><li>PASSENGER SEAT BELT ANCHOR PRETENSIONER</li><li>OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER (ORC)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM PRE-DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read ORC DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Record the Environmental Data.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using the recorded Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read ORC DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM INTERMITTENT TEST . Probing of the circuit cavities at the ORC Module body harness connectors or vehicle connectors is only to be done with a approved test lead from the test lead 10159-6 or the use of Breakout Box 8443-55 to prevent vehicle wiring harness connector damage during diagnostic procedures.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK FOR OPEN PASSENGER SEAT BELT BUCKLE TENSIONER</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition off disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the Passenger Seat Belt Buckle Tensioner harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:            Check the connectors - Clean and repair as necessary.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Connect the (special tool #8443A, SRS Load Tool) and the (special tool #8443-8, Jumper, SRS Load) to the Passenger Seat Belt Buckle Tensioner harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the standard key ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition on, then reconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the keyless ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Disconnect the 12-volt battery wait two minutes before proceeding, remove the ORC fuses, connect the 12-volt battery, wait two minutes before proceeding. Cycle the ignition to the On position, then reconnect the ORC fuses. Wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read the active ORC DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Does the scan tool display: B0072-13-PASSENGER SEATBELT BUCKLE PRETENSIONER - CIRCUIT OPEN?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Replace the Passenger Seat Belt Buckle Tensioner in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to BUCKLE, SEAT BELT, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK (R56) PASSENGER SEAT BELT BUCKLE TENSIONER LINE 1 CIRCUIT AND (R54) PASSENGER SEAT BELT BUCKLE TENSIONER LINE 2 CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition off disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the (special tool #8443A, SRS Load Tool) and the (special tool #8443-8, Jumper, SRS Load) from the Passenger Seat Belt Buckle Tensioner harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the ORC harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Check the connectors - Clean and repair as necessary.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Connect the test leads to the DVOM.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (R54) Passenger Seat Belt Buckle Tensioner Line 1 circuit between the Passenger Seat Belt Tensioner harness connector terminal 1 and the ORC Module body harness connector terminal C2-82.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (R56) Passenger Seat Belt Buckle Tensioner Line 2 circuit between the Passenger Seat Belt Tensioner harness connector terminal 2 and the ORC Module body harness connector terminal C2-81.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Is the resistance below 1.0 Ohm for both circuits?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:       If the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) is dropped at any time, it must be replaced. Failure to take the proper precautions can result in accidental airbag deployment. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the ORC in accordance with Service Information. Refer to MODULE, OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the open (R54) or (R56) Passenger Seat Belt Buckle Tensioner circuits.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b0072-2b passenger seatbelt buckle pretensioner wires shorted together\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B0072-2B</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">PASSENGER SEATBELT BUCKLE PRETENSIONER WIRES SHORTED TOGETHER</small><small>العطل: قصر بين الأسلاك</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">When powered, the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) sends a test current to the squibs to verify the</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">integrity of the squib and wiring. These circuits are maintained in a &quot;floating&quot; configuration at the module (connected to neither power nor ground) as protection against inadvertent deployment.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) monitors the squib circuits for multiple circuit failures. If the controller detects a circuit value that is out of the allowable range, the ORC will set this DTC.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">In the case that this DTC is set, the squib may still deploy in a crash event.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>PASSENGER SEAT BELT ANCHOR TENSIONER LINE 1 CIRCUIT SHORTED TO THE</li><li>PASSENGER SEAT BELT ANCHOR TENSIONER LINE 2 CIRCUIT</li><li>PASSENGER SEAT BELT ANCHOR TENSIONER</li><li>OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER (ORC)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM PRE-DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read ORC DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Record the Environmental Data.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using the recorded Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read ORC DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM INTERMITTENT TEST . Probing of the circuit cavities at the ORC Module body harness connectors or vehicle connectors is only to be done with a approved test lead from the test lead 10159-6 or the use of Breakout Box 8443-55 to prevent vehicle wiring harness connector damage during diagnostic procedures.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK FOR SHORTED PASSENGER SEAT BELT BUCKLE PRETENSIONER</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition off disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the Passenger Seat Belt Tensioner harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Check the connectors - Clean and repair as necessary.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Connect the (special tool #8443A, SRS Load Tool) and the (special tool #8443-8, Jumper, SRS Load) to the Passenger Seat Belt Tensioner harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the standard key ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition on, then reconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the keyless ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Disconnect the 12-volt battery wait two minutes before proceeding, remove the ORC fuses, connect the 12-volt battery, wait two minutes before proceeding. Cycle the ignition to the On position, then reconnect the ORC fuses. Wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read the active ORC DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Does the scan tool display: B0072-2B-PASSENGER SEATBELT BUCKLE PRETENSIONER - WIRES SHORTED TOGETHER?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Replace the Passenger Seat Belt Buckle Pretensioner in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to BUCKLE, SEAT BELT, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK (R56) PASSENGER SEAT BELT BUCKLE TENSIONER LINE 1 CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO (R54) PASSENGER SEAT BELT BUCKLE TENSIONER LINE 2 CIRCUIT</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition off disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the (special tool #8443A, SRS Load Tool) and the (special tool #8443-8, Jumper, SRS Load) from the Passenger Seat Belt Buckle Tensioner harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the ORC harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          Check the connectors - Clean and repair as necessary.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Connect the test leads to the DVOM.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Measure the resistance between the (R56) Passenger Seat Belt Buckle Pretensioner Line 1 circuit at the ORC Module body harness connector terminal C2-81 and the (R54) Passenger Seat Belt Buckle Tensioner Line 2 circuit at the ORC Module body harness connector terminal C2-82.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Is the resistance below 10K Ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Repair the (R56) Passenger Seat Belt Buckle Tensioner Line 1 circuit for a short to the (R54) Passenger Seat Belt Buckle Tensioner Line 2 circuit.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:       If the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) is dropped at any time, it must be replaced. Failure to take the proper precautions can result in accidental airbag deployment. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Replace the ORC in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b0072-95 passenger seatbelt buckle pretensioner incorrect assembly\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B0072-95</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">PASSENGER SEATBELT BUCKLE PRETENSIONER INCORRECT ASSEMBLY</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">When powered, the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) sends a test current to the SeatBelt Buckle Pretensioner sensors. During this test, the sensors discovered are checked for agreement with the pre- programmed configuration of components assigned to the module.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs once during the initialization process.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">With the ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This DTC sets when the ORC detects the presence of a Seatbelt Buckle Pretensioner sensor circuit while the configuration of the module does not reflect a SeatBelt Buckle Pretensioner sensor should be present. Once set, this DTC is latched for the entire power cycle and requires the module to be re-initalized to set code.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This DTC may inhibit deployment or modify deployment strategy.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>UNUSED SEAT BELT BUCKLE PRETENSIONER SENSOR CIRCUITS SHORTED TO VOLTAGE,</li><li>SHORTED TO GROUND, OR SHORTED TOGETHER</li><li>OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER (ORC)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM PRE-DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read ORC DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Record the Environmental Data.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using the recorded Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read ORC DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM INTERMITTENT TEST . Probing of the circuit cavities at the ORC Module body harness connectors or vehicle connectors is only to be done with a approved test lead from the test lead 10159-6 or the use of Breakout Box 8443-55 to prevent vehicle wiring harness connector damage during diagnostic procedures.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK UNUSED SEAT BELT BUCKLE PRETENSIONER SENSOR CIRCUITS FOR A SHORT TO VOLTAGE, SHORT TO GROUND, OR SHORT TOGETHER</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check any unused Seat Belt Buckle Pretensioner Sensor circuits for possible short to voltage.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Check any unused Seat Belt Buckle Pretensioner Sensor circuits for possible short to ground.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Check any unused Seat Belt Buckle Pretensioner Sensor circuits for possible short together.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are any of the unused Seat Belt Buckle Pretensioner Sensor circuits shorted?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition off disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair any unused Seat Belt Buckle Pretensioner Sensor circuits that are shorted.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM INTERMITTENT TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:        Ensure the part number of the replacement module is the correct part number for the vehicle.</div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:     If the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) is dropped at any time, it must be replaced. Failure to take the proper precautions can result in accidental airbag deployment. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:     Turn the ignition off disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Replace the ORC in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b0072-9a passenger seatbelt buckle pretensioner component or system\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B0072-9A</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">PASSENGER SEATBELT BUCKLE PRETENSIONER COMPONENT OR SYSTEM</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">OPERATING CONDITIONS</p></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">When powered, the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) sends a test current to the SeatBelt Buckle Pretensioners to verify the integrity of the Pretensioner and wiring. The presence of this code indicates that any two circuits, from two or more Pretensioners, have become shorted or &quot;coupled&quot; together.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The ORC checks the squib circuits once during the initialization process.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Module detects that two squib lines from separate circuits are coupled together.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Once set, the DTC is latched for the entire power cycle and requires the module to be re-initialized to transition code from active to stored. This DTC may inhibit deployment or modify deployment strategy.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>2 SQUIB LINES FROM SEPARATE CIRCUITS COUPLED TOGETHER</li><li>OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER (ORC)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM PRE-DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>DETERMINE ACTIVE OR STORED DTC</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:            Make sure the battery is fully charged.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Perform ORC module reset. Access the Miscellaneous Function menu from the ORC ECU Overview screen on the scan tool to perform this operation.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Using the scan tool, read ORC DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active or stored?</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">ORC - ACTIVE DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLE CODE (DTC)</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Go To 2</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">ORC - STORED DTC</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM INTERMITTENT TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK FOR ADDITIONAL ACTIVE SQUIB DTCS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Using the scan tool, read ORC DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are there squib specific DTCs set as active in addition to B0072-9A-PASSENGER SEATBELT BUCKLE PRETENSIONER - COMPONENT OR SYSTEM OPERATING CONDITIONS?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair all other active squib specific DTCs before repairing B0072-9A-PASSENGER SEATBELT BUCKLE PRETENSIONER - COMPONENT OR SYSTEM OPERATING CONDITIONS.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>USE THE SCAN TOOL TO IDENTIFY THE COUPLED CIRCUITS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Using the scan tool, identify the two or more sensor circuits that read SET.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are two or more sensor circuits DTCs set?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the two or more sensor circuits for a sensor Circuit Coupling condition.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM INTERMITTENT TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b007f-11 passenger seatbelt retractor pretensioner circuit short to\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B007F-11</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">PASSENGER SEATBELT RETRACTOR PRETENSIONER CIRCUIT SHORT TO</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">GROUND</p></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">When powered, the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) sends a test current to the squibs to verify the integrity of the squib and wiring. These circuits are maintained in a &quot;floating&quot; configuration at the module (connected to neither power nor ground) as protection against inadvertent deployment.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) monitors the squib circuits for multiple circuit failures. If the controller detects a circuit value that is out of the allowable range, the ORC will set this DTC.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">In the case that this DTC is set, the squib may still deploy in a crash event.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>PASSENGER RETRACTOR PRETENSIONER LINE 2 CIRCUIT SHORTED TO GROUND</li><li>PASSENGER RETRACTOR PRETENSIONER LINE 1 CIRCUIT SHORTED TO GROUND</li><li>PASSENGER RETRACTOR PRETENSIONER</li><li>OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER (ORC)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM PRE-DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read ORC DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Record the Environmental Data.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using the recorded Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read ORC DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM INTERMITTENT TEST . Probing of the circuit cavities at the ORC Module body harness connectors or vehicle connectors is only to be done with a approved test lead from the test lead 10159-6 or the use of Breakout Box 8443-55 to prevent vehicle wiring harness connector damage during diagnostic procedures.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK FOR SHORTED PASSENGER SEAT BELT RETRACTOR PRETENSIONER</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:      Turn the ignition off, disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the Passenger Seat Belt Retractor Pretensioner harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Do not place an intact undeployed airbag face down on a hard surface, the airbag will propel into the air if accidentally deployed. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Check connectors - Clean and repair as necessary.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Connect the (special tool #8443A, SRS Load Tool) (special tool #8443-8, Jumper, SRS Load) to the Passenger Seat Belt Retractor Pretensioner harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the standard key ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition on, then reconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the keyless ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Disconnect the 12-volt battery wait two minutes before proceeding, remove the ORC fuses, connect the 12-volt battery, wait two minutes before proceeding. Cycle the ignition to the On position, then reconnect the ORC fuses. Wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read the active ORC DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Does the scan tool display: B007F-11-PASSENGER SEATBELT RETRACTOR PRETENSIONER - CIRCUIT SHORT TO GROUND?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition off, disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Replace the Passenger Seat Belt Retractor Tensioner in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to RETRACTOR, SEAT BELT, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK (R506) PASSENGER SEAT BELT RETRACTOR PRETENSIONER AND (R504) PASSENGER SEAT BELT RETRACTOR PRETENSIONER LINE 2 CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO GROUND</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition off, disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the (special tool #8443A, SRS Load Tool) (special tool #8443-8, Jumper, SRS Load) from the Passenger Seat Belt Retractor Pretensioner harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the ORC harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Check the connectors - Clean and repair as necessary.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Connect the test leads to the DVOM.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (R506) Passenger Seat Belt Retractor Tensioner Line 1 circuit</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">between ground and the ORC module body harness connector terminal C2-95.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (R504) Passenger Seat Belt Retractor Tensioner Line 2 circuit between ground and the ORC module body harness connector terminal C2-96.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance below 5K Ohms on either circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair or replace the Passenger Seat Belt Retractor Pretensioner circuits with a resistance below 5K Ohms in accordance with the Service Information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        If the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) is dropped at any time, it must be replaced. Failure to take the proper precautions can result in accidental airbag deployment. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the ORC in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>STORED ORC DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, record and erase all DTCs from all Airbag System Modules.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>If any ACTIVE codes are present they must be resolved before diagnosing any stored codes.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition off, disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Using the wiring diagram/schematic as a guide, inspect the wiring and connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Look for chafed, pierced, pinched, or partially broken wires and broken, bent, pushed out, spread, corroded, or contaminated terminals.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>The following additional checks may assist you in identifying a possible intermittent problem.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Reconnect any disconnected components and harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the standard key ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition on, then reconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the keyless ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Disconnect the 12-volt battery wait two minutes before proceeding, remove the ORC fuses, connect the 12-volt battery, wait two minutes before proceeding. Cycle the ignition to the On position, then reconnect the ORC fuses. Wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>With the scan tool monitor active codes as you work through the following steps.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">10</span><span>Wiggle the wiring harness and connectors of the related airbag circuit or component.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">11</span><span>If codes are related to the Driver Airbag circuits, rotate the steering wheel from stop to stop.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">12</span><span>If only stored codes return continue the test until the problem area has been isolated.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">13</span><span>In the previous steps you have attempted to recreate the conditions responsible for setting active DTC in question.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Are any ACTIVE DTCs present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Select the appropriate diagnostic procedure. Refer to DTC INDEX .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">No problem found at this time. Erase all codes before returning vehicle to customer.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b007f-12 passenger seatbelt retractor-circuit short to battery\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B007F-12</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">PASSENGER SEATBELT RETRACTOR-CIRCUIT SHORT TO BATTERY</small><small>العطل: قصر على البطارية</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">When powered, the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) sends a test current to the squibs to verify the integrity of the squib and wiring. These circuits are maintained in a &quot;floating&quot; configuration at the module (connected to neither power nor ground) as protection against inadvertent deployment.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) monitors the squib circuits for multiple circuit failures. If the controller detects a circuit value that is out of the allowable range, the ORC will set this DTC.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">In the case that this DTC is set, the squib may still deploy in a crash event.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>PASSENGER SEAT BELT RETRACTOR PRETENSIONER LINE 2 CIRCUIT SHORTED TO</li><li>VOLTAGE</li><li>PASSENGER SEAT BELT RETRACTOR PRETENSIONER LINE 1 CIRCUIT SHORTED TO</li><li>VOLTAGE</li><li>PASSENGER SEAT BELT RETRACTOR PRETENSIONER</li><li>OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER (ORC)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM PRE-DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read ORC DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Record the Environmental Data.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using the recorded Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read ORC DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM INTERMITTENT TEST . Probing of the circuit cavities at the ORC Module body harness connectors or vehicle connectors is only to be done with a approved test lead from the test lead 10159-6 or the use of Breakout Box 8443-55 to prevent vehicle wiring harness connector damage during diagnostic procedures.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK FOR SHORTED PASSENGER SEAT BELT RETRACTOR PRETENSIONER</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:       Turn the ignition off, disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the Passenger Seat Belt Retractor Pretensioner harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Do not place an intact undeployed airbag face down on a hard surface, the airbag will propel into the air if accidentally deployed. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Check connectors - Clean and repair as necessary.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Connect the (special tool #8443A, SRS Load Tool) (special tool #8443-8, Jumper, SRS Load) to the Passenger Seat Belt Retractor Pretensioner harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the standard key ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition on, then reconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the keyless ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Disconnect the 12-volt battery wait two minutes before proceeding, remove the ORC fuses, connect the 12-volt battery, wait two minutes before proceeding. Cycle the ignition to the On position, then reconnect the ORC fuses. Wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read the active ORC DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the scan tool display: B007F-12-PASSENGER SEATBELT RETRACTOR - CIRCUIT SHORT TO BATTERY?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition off, disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Replace the Passenger Seat Belt Retractor Pretensioner in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to RETRACTOR, SEAT BELT, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK (R506) PASSENGER SEAT BELT RETRACTOR PRETENSIONER AND (R504) PASSENGER SEAT BELT RETRACTOR PRETENSIONER FOR A SHORT TO VOLTAGE</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:       Turn the ignition off, disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the (special tool #8443A, SRS Load Tool) (special tool #8443-8, Jumper, SRS Load) from the Passenger Seat Belt Retractor Pretensioner harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the ORC harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:            Check the connectors - Clean and repair as necessary.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Connect the test leads to the DVOM.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the standard key ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:         Turn the ignition on, then reconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the keyless ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:         Disconnect the 12-volt battery wait two minutes before proceeding, remove the ORC fuses, connect the 12-volt battery, wait two minutes before proceeding. Cycle the ignition to the On position, then reconnect the ORC fuses. Wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Measure the voltage of the (R506) Passenger Seat Belt Retractor Tensioner Line 1 circuit between the Passenger Seat Belt Retractor Pretensioner connector and ground at the ORC module body harness connector terminal C2-95.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Measure the voltage of the (R504) Passenger Seat Belt Retractor Tensioner Line 2 circuit between the Passenger Seat Belt Retractor Pretensioner connector and ground at the ORC module body harness connector terminal C2-96.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there any voltage present on either circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair or replace the Passenger Seat Belt Retractor Pretensioner circuits with voltage present in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to RETRACTOR, SEAT BELT, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:         If the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) is dropped at any time, it must be replaced. Failure to take the proper precautions can result in accidental airbag deployment. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:         Turn the ignition off, disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the ORC in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>STORED ORC DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, record and erase all DTCs from all Airbag System Modules.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>If any ACTIVE codes are present they must be resolved before diagnosing any stored codes.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:         Turn the ignition off, disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Using the wiring diagram/schematic as a guide, inspect the wiring and connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Look for chafed, pierced, pinched, or partially broken wires and broken, bent, pushed out, spread, corroded, or contaminated terminals.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>The following additional checks may assist you in identifying a possible intermittent problem.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Reconnect any disconnected components and harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the standard key ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:         Turn the ignition on, then reconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the keyless ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:         Disconnect the 12-volt battery wait two minutes before proceeding, remove the ORC fuses, connect the 12-volt battery, wait two minutes before proceeding. Cycle the ignition to the On position, then reconnect the ORC fuses. Wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>With the scan tool monitor active codes as you work through the following steps.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">10</span><span>Wiggle the wiring harness and connectors of the related airbag circuit or component.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">11</span><span>If codes are related to the Driver Airbag circuits, rotate the steering wheel from stop to stop.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">12</span><span>If only stored codes return continue the test until the problem area has been isolated.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">13</span><span>In the previous steps you have attempted to recreate the conditions responsible for setting active DTC in question.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are any ACTIVE DTCs present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Select the appropriate diagnostic procedure. Refer to DTC INDEX .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">No problem found at this time. Erase all codes before returning vehicle to customer.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b007f-13 passenger seatbelt retractor pretensioner circuit open\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B007F-13</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">PASSENGER SEATBELT RETRACTOR PRETENSIONER CIRCUIT OPEN</small><small>العطل: دائرة مفتوحة</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">When powered, the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) sends a test current to the squibs to verify the integrity of the squib and wiring. These circuits are maintained in a &quot;floating&quot; configuration at the module (connected to neither power nor ground) as protection against inadvertent deployment.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) monitors the squib circuits for multiple circuit failures. If the controller detects a circuit value that is out of the allowable range, the ORC will set this DTC.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">In the case that this DTC is set, the squib may still deploy in a crash event.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>PASSENGER SEAT BELT RETRACTOR PRETENSIONER LINE 2 CIRCUIT OPEN</li><li>PASSENGER SEAT BELT RETRACTOR PRETENSIONER LINE 1 CIRCUIT OPEN</li><li>PASSENGER SEAT BELT RETRACTOR PRETENSIONER</li><li>OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER (ORC)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM PRE-DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read ORC DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Record the Environmental Data.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using the recorded Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read ORC DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM INTERMITTENT TEST . Probing of the circuit cavities at the ORC Module body harness connectors or vehicle connectors is only to be done with a approved test lead from the test lead 10159-6 or the use of Breakout Box 8443-55 to prevent vehicle wiring harness connector damage during diagnostic procedures.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK FOR PASSENGER SEAT BELT RETRACTOR PRETENSIONER CIRCUIT OPEN</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:         Turn the ignition off, disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">possible serious or fatal injury.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the Passenger Seat Belt Retractor Pretensioner connector.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Check the connectors - Clean and repair as necessary.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Connect the (special tool #8443A, SRS Load Tool) and the(special tool #8443-8, Jumper, SRS Load) to the Passenger Seat Belt Retractor Pretensioner connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the standard key ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition on, then reconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the keyless ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Disconnect the 12-volt battery wait two minutes before proceeding, remove the ORC fuses, connect the 12-volt battery, wait two minutes before proceeding. Cycle the ignition to the On position, then reconnect the ORC fuses. Wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read the active ORC DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Does the scan tool display: B007F-13-PASSENGER SEATBELT RETRACTOR PRETENSIONER - CIRCUIT OPEN?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition off, disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Replace the Passenger Seat Belt Retractor Pretensioner in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to RETRACTOR, SEAT BELT, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the RESTRAINT SYSTEMS VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to STANDARD PROCEDURE .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK (R506) PASSENGER SEAT BELT RETRACTOR PRETENSIONER LINE 1 CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition off, disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the(special tool #8443A, SRS Load Tool) and the(special tool #8443-8, Jumper, SRS</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Load) from the Passenger Seat Belt Retractor Pretensioner harness connector.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the ORC harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          Check the connectors - Clean and repair as necessary.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Connect the test leads to the DVOM.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (R506) Passenger Seat Belt Retractor Pretensioner Line 1 circuit between the Passenger Seat Belt Retractor Pretensioner connector terminal 1 and the ORC module body harness connector terminal C2-95.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance below 1.0 Ohm?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair or replace the (R506) Passenger Seat Belt Retractor Pretensioner Line 1 circuit in accordance with the Service Information. Then Go To</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK (R504) PASSENGER SEAT BELT RETRACTOR PRETENSIONER LINE 2 CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (R504) Passenger Seat Belt Retractor Pretensioner Line 2 circuit between the Passenger Seat Belt Retractor Pretensioner connector terminal 2 and the ORC module body harness connector terminal C2-96.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance below 1.0 Ohm?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:       If the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) is dropped at any time, it must be replaced. Failure to take the proper precautions can result in accidental airbag deployment and serious or fatal injury.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the ORC in accordance with Service Information. Refer to MODULE, OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair or replace the (R504) Passenger Seat Belt Retractor Pretensioner Line 2 circuit for and open in accordance with the Service Information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b007f-2b passenger seatbelt retractor pretensioner wires shorted\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B007F-2B</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">PASSENGER SEATBELT RETRACTOR PRETENSIONER WIRES SHORTED</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">TOGETHER</p></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">When powered, the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) sends a test current to the squibs to verify the integrity of the squib and wiring. These circuits are maintained in a &quot;floating&quot; configuration at the module (connected to neither power nor ground) as protection against inadvertent deployment.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) monitors the squib circuits for multiple circuit failures. If the controller detects a circuit value that is out of the allowable range, the ORC will set this DTC.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">In the case that this DTC is set, the squib may still deploy in a crash event.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>PASSENGER SEAT BELT RETRACTOR PRETENSIONER LINE 2 CIRCUIT SHORTED TO THE</li><li>PASSENGER SEAT BELT RETRACTOR PRETENSIONER LINE 1</li><li>PASSENGER SEAT BELT RETRACTOR TENSIONER</li><li>OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER (ORC)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM PRE-DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read ORC DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Record the Environmental Data.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using the recorded Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read ORC DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM INTERMITTENT TEST . Probing of the circuit cavities at the ORC Module body harness connectors or vehicle connectors is only to be done with a approved test lead from the test lead 10159-6 or the use of Breakout Box 8443-55 to prevent vehicle wiring harness connector damage during diagnostic procedures.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK FOR SHORTED PASSENGER SEAT BELT RETRACTOR PRETENSIONER</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:      Turn the ignition off, disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the Passenger Seatbelt Retractor Pretensioner harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Check connectors - Clean and repair as necessary.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Connect the(special tool #8443A, SRS Load Tool) and the (special tool #8443-8, Jumper, SRS Load) to the Passenger Seat Belt Retractor Pretensioner harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the standard key ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition on, then reconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the keyless ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Disconnect the 12-volt battery wait two minutes before proceeding, remove the ORC fuses, connect the 12-volt battery, wait two minutes before proceeding. Cycle the ignition to the On position, then reconnect the ORC fuses. Wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read the active ORC DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Does the scan tool display: B007F-2B-PASSENGER SEATBELT RETRACTOR PRETENSIONER - WIRES SHORTED TOGETHER?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition off, disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Passenger Seat Belt Retractor Tensioner in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to RETRACTOR, SEAT BELT, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK (R506) PASSENGER SEAT BELT RETRACTOR PRETENSIONER FOR A SHORT TO THE (R504) PASSENGER SEAT BELT RETRACTOR PRETENSIONER</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition off, disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the (special tool #8443A, SRS Load Tool) and the (special tool #8443-8, Jumper, SRS Load) from the Passenger Seat Belt Retractor Pretensioner harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the ORC harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Check the connectors - Clean and repair as necessary.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Connect the test leads to the DVOM.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Measure the resistance between the (R506) Passenger Seat Belt Retractor Pretensioner Line 1 circuit terminal C2-95 and the (R504) Passenger Seat Belt Retractor Pretensioner Line 2 circuit terminal C2-96 at the ORC module body harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Is the resistance below 5K Ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair or replace the (R506) Passenger Seat Belt Retractor Pretensioner Line 1 circuit for a short to the (R504) Passenger Seat Belt Retractor Pretensioner Line 2 circuit in accordance with the Service Information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        If the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) is dropped at any time, it must be replaced. Failure to take the proper precautions can result in accidental airbag deployment. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the ORC in accordance with Service Information. Refer to MODULE, OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>STORED ORC DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, record and erase all DTCs from all Airbag System Modules.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>If any ACTIVE codes are present they must be resolved before diagnosing any stored codes.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition off, disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Using the wiring diagram/schematic as a guide, inspect the wiring and connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Look for chafed, pierced, pinched, or partially broken wires and broken, bent, pushed out, spread, corroded, or contaminated terminals.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>The following additional checks may assist you in identifying a possible intermittent problem.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Reconnect any disconnected components and harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the standard key ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition on, then reconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the keyless ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Disconnect the 12-volt battery wait two minutes before proceeding, remove the ORC fuses, connect the 12-volt battery, wait two minutes before proceeding. Cycle the ignition to the On position, then reconnect the ORC fuses. Wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>With the scan tool monitor active codes as you work through the following steps.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Maintain a safe distance from all airbags while performing the following steps. Failure to follow these instructions may result in</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">possible serious or fatal injury.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">10</span><span>Wiggle the wiring harness and connectors of the related airbag circuit or component.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">11</span><span>If codes are related to the Driver Airbag circuits, rotate the steering wheel from stop to stop.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">12</span><span>If only stored codes return continue the test until the problem area has been isolated.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">13</span><span>In the previous steps you have attempted to recreate the conditions responsible for setting active DTC in question.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Are any ACTIVE DTCs present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Select the appropriate diagnostic procedure. Refer to DTC INDEX .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">No problem found at this time. Erase all codes before returning vehicle to customer.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b007f-95 passenger seatbelt retractor pretensioner incorrect assembly\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B007F-95</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">PASSENGER SEATBELT RETRACTOR PRETENSIONER INCORRECT ASSEMBLY</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">When powered, the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) sends a test current to the Seatbelt Retractor</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Pretensioner Sensors. During this test, the sensors discovered are checked for agreement with the pre- programmed configuration of components assigned to the module.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs once during the initialization process.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">With the ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This DTC sets when the ORC detects the presence of a seatbelt retractor pretensioner sensor circuit while the configuration of the module does not reflect a Seatbelt Retractor Pretensioner Sensor should be present. Once set, this DTC is latched for the entire power cycle and requires the module to be re- initalized to set code.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This DTC may inhibit deployment or modify deployment strategy.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>UNUSED SEATBELT RETRACTOR PRETENSIONER SENSOR CIRCUITS SHORTED TO</li><li>VOLTAGE, SHORTED TO GROUND, OR SHORTED TOGETHER</li><li>OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER (ORC)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM PRE-DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read ORC DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Record the Environmental Data.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using the recorded Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read ORC DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM INTERMITTENT TEST . Probing of the circuit cavities at the ORC Module body harness connectors or vehicle connectors is only to be done with a approved test lead from the test lead 10159-6 or the use of Breakout Box 8443-55 to prevent vehicle wiring harness connector damage during diagnostic procedures.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK UNUSED SEATBELT RETRACTOR PRETENSIONER SENSOR CIRCUITS FOR A SHORT TO VOLTAGE, SHORT TO GROUND, OR SHORT TOGETHER</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check any unused SeatBelt Retractor Pretensioner Sensor circuits for possible short to voltage.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Check any unused SeatBelt Retractor Pretensioner Sensor circuits for possible short to ground.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Check any unused SeatBelt Retractor Pretensioner Sensor circuits for possible short together.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are any of the unused SeatBelt Retractor Pretensioner circuits shorted?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition off disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair any unused SeatBelt Retractor Pretensioner Sensor circuits that are shorted.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM INTERMITTENT TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Make sure the part number of the replacement module is the correct part number for the vehicle.</div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        If the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) is dropped at any time, it must be replaced. Failure to take the proper precautions can result in accidental airbag deployment. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition off disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the ORC in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b007f-9a passenger seatbelt retractor pretensioner component or system\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B007F-9A</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">PASSENGER SEATBELT RETRACTOR PRETENSIONER COMPONENT OR SYSTEM</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">OPERATING CONDITIONS</p></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">When powered, the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) sends a test current to the seatbelt retractor pretensioner sensor to verify the integrity of the sensor and wiring. The presence of this code indicates that any two circuits, from two or more sensors, have become shorted or &quot;coupled&quot; together.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The ORC checks the squib circuits once during the initialization process.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Module detects that two squib lines from separate circuits are coupled together.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Once set, the DTC is latched for the entire power cycle and requires the module to be re-initialized to transition code from active to stored. This DTC may inhibit deployment or modify deployment strategy.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>2 SQUIB LINES FROM SEPARATE CIRCUITS COUPLED TOGETHER</li><li>OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER (ORC)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM PRE-DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>DETERMINE ACTIVE OR STORED DTC</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Make sure the battery is fully charged.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Perform ORC module reset. Access the Miscellaneous Function menu from the ORC ECU Overview screen on the scan tool to perform this operation.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Using the scan tool, read ORC DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active or stored?</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">ORC - ACTIVE DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLE CODE (DTC)</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">ORC - STORED DTC</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM INTERMITTENT TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK FOR ADDITIONAL ACTIVE SENSOR DTCS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Using the scan tool, read ORC DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are there squib specific DTCs set as active in addition to B007F-9A-PASSENGER SEATBELT RETRACTOR PRETENSIONER - COMPONENT OR SYSTEM OPERATING CONDITIONS?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair all other active sensor specific DTCs before repairing B007F-9A-PASSENGER SEATBELT RETRACTOR PRETENSIONER - COMPONENT OR SYSTEM OPERATING CONDITIONS.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>USE THE SCAN TOOL TO IDENTIFY THE COUPLED CIRCUITS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Using the scan tool, identify the two or more sensor circuits that read SET.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are two or more sensor circuits DTCs set?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the two or more sensor circuits for a Sensor Circuit Coupling condition.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM INTERMITTENT TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b0090-11 left frontal acceleration sensor circuit short to ground\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B0090-11</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">LEFT FRONTAL ACCELERATION SENSOR CIRCUIT SHORT TO GROUND</small><small>العطل: قصر على الأرضي</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">When powered, the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) sends a test current to the Impact/Pressure Sensors to verify the integrity of the sensor and wiring.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) monitors the Impact/Pressure Sensor circuits for multiple circuit failures. If the controller detects a circuit value that is out of the allowable range, the ORC will set this DTC.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This DTC may or may not allow the squib to deploy during a crash event.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>LEFT FRONT IMPACT SENSOR SIGNAL CIRCUITS SHORTED TO GROUND</li><li>LEFT FRONT IMPACT SENSOR CIRCUITS SHORTED TOGETHER</li><li>LEFT FRONT IMPACT SENSOR</li><li>OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER (ORC)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM PRE-DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>DETERMINE ACTIVE OR STORED DTC</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          The use of a approved special tool or Digital Multimeter such as a Fluke Meter that will not apply more than 20 milliamperes to a circuit are the only measurement tools to be used.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          Probing of the circuit cavities at the ORC Module C1-A, C1-B, or C2-A body harness connectors is only to be done with a approved test lead from the Dedicated Test Leads kit 10159, test lead 10159-6. Or a comparable test lead to prevent vehicle wiring harness connector damage during diagnostic procedures. (special tool #10159, Test Leads, Dedicated)</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          Make sure the battery is fully charged.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read ORC DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Does the scan tool display active: B0090-11-LEFT FRONTAL RESTRAINTS SENSOR -CIRCUIT SHORT TO GROUND?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM INTERMITTENT TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE (R79, R81) FRONT LEFT IMPACT SENSOR SIGNAL AND GROUND CIRCUITS FOR A SHORT TO VOLTAGE</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:      Turn the ignition off, disconnect the battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the Front Left Impact Sensor harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the ORC harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the standard key ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition on, then reconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the keyless ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Disconnect the 12-volt battery wait two minutes before proceeding, remove the ORC fuses, connect the 12-volt battery, wait two minutes before proceeding. Cycle the ignition to the On position, then reconnect the ORC fuses. Wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">fatal injury.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Measure the voltage of the (R79) Front Left Impact Sensor Signal circuit and (R81) Sensor Ground circuit at the Front Left Impact Sensor connector and ground.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Is there any voltage present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (R79, R81) Front Left Impact Sensor circuits for a short to voltage.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (R79, R81) FRONT LEFT IMPACT SENSOR SIGNAL CIRCUITS FOR A SHORT TO GROUND</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:      Turn the ignition off, disconnect the battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (R79, 81) Front Left Impact Sensor Signal circuits between the Front</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Left Impact Sensor connector and ground.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Is the resistance below 100K Ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (R79, R81) Front Left Impact Sensor Signal circuits for a short to ground.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Go To 4</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK THE (R79, R81) FRONT LEFT IMPACT SENSOR CIRCUITS FOR A SHORT TOGETHER</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Measure the resistance between the (R79) Front Left Impact Sensor Signal and (R81) Sensor Ground circuits at the Front Left Impact Sensor harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Is the resistance below 100K Ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (R79, R81) Front Left Impact Sensor circuits shorted together.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Go To 5</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>CHECK THE (R81) FRONT LEFT IMPACT SENSOR GROUND CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN OR HIGH RESISTANCE</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:       Turn the ignition off, disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the ORC Module body harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Connect the test leads to the DVOM.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (R81) Front Left Impact Sensor Ground circuit between the Front Left Impact Sensor connector terminal 2 and the ORC Module body harness connector terminal C1-14.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance below 1 Ohm?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 6</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (R81) Front Left Impact Sensor Ground circuit for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>CHECK THE (R79) FRONT LEFT IMPACT SENSOR CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN OR HIGH RESISTANCE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (R79) Front Left Impact Sensor Signal circuit between the Front Left Impact Sensor connector terminal 1 and the ORC Module body harness connector terminal C1-13.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance below 1 Ohm?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 7</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (R79) Front Left Impact Sensor Signal circuit for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>CHECK OPERATION OF THE FRONT LEFT IMPACT SENSOR</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Replace the Front Left Impact Sensor in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to SENSOR, IMPACT, REMOVAL .</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Reconnect the vehicle body harness to the impact sensor.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Remove any special tools or jumper wires and reconnect all previously disconnected components - except the Battery.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the standard key ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition on, then reconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the keyless ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Disconnect the 12-volt battery wait two minutes before proceeding, remove the ORC fuses, connect the 12-volt battery, wait two minutes before proceeding. Cycle the ignition to the On position, then reconnect the ORC fuses. Wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Connect the scan tool to the Data Link Connector - use the most current software available.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Use the scan tool and erase the stored codes in all airbag system modules.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>Turn the Ignition Off, and wait 15 seconds before turning the Ignition On.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>Wait one minute, and read active codes and if there are none present read the stored codes.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Did the active Front Left Impact Sensor DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 8</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Repair is complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>CHECK RELATED HARNESS CONNECTIONS</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:       Turn the ignition off, disconnect the battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:       If the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) is dropped at any time, it must be replaced. Failure to take the proper precautions could result in accidental airbag deployment. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect all Occupant Restraint Controller(ORC) harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect all related in-line harness connections (if equipped).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Disconnect the related component harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Inspect harness connectors, component connectors, and all male and female terminals for the following conditions: Proper connector installation. Damaged connector locks. Corrosion. Other signs of water intrusion. Weather seal damage (if equipped). Bent terminals. Overheating due to a poor connection (terminal may be discolored due to excessive current draw). Terminals that have been pushed back into the connector cavity. Check for spread terminals and verify proper terminal tension.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Repair any conditions that are found.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Connect all Occupant Restraint Controller(ORC) harness connectors. Be certain that all harness connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Connect all in-line harness connectors (if equipped). Be certain that all connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Connect all related component harness connectors. Be certain that all connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>Test drive or operate the vehicle in accordance with the when monitored and set conditions.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">10</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Replace and program the Occupant Restraint Controller in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to STANDARD PROCEDURE .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">The wiring or poor connection problem has been repaired.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the Occupant Restraint Controller VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to STANDARD PROCEDURE .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b0090-12 left frontal acceleration sensor circuit short to battery\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B0090-12</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">LEFT FRONTAL ACCELERATION SENSOR CIRCUIT SHORT TO BATTERY</small><small>العطل: قصر على البطارية</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">When powered, the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) sends a test current to the Impact/Pressure Sensors to verify the integrity of the sensor and wiring.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) monitors the Impact/Pressure Sensor circuits for multiple circuit failures. If the controller detects a circuit value that is out of the allowable range, the ORC will set this DTC.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This DTC may or may not allow the squib to deploy during a crash event.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>LEFT FRONT IMPACT SENSOR SIGNAL CIRCUITS SHORTED TO VOLTAGE</li><li>LEFT FRONT IMPACT SENSOR CIRCUITS SHORTED TOGETHER</li><li>LEFT FRONT IMPACT SENSOR</li><li>OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER (ORC)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM PRE-DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read ORC DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Record the Environmental Data.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using the recorded Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read ORC DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM INTERMITTENT TEST . Probing of the circuit cavities at the ORC Module body harness connectors or vehicle connectors is only to be done with a approved test lead from the test lead 10159-6 or the use of Breakout Box 8443-55 to prevent vehicle wiring harness connector damage during diagnostic procedures.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE (R79, R81) FRONT LEFT IMPACT SENSOR SIGNAL AND GROUND CIRCUITS FOR A SHORT CIRCUITS</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:      Turn the ignition off, disconnect the battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the Front Left Impact Sensor harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the ORC Module harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the standard key ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition on, then reconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the keyless ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Disconnect the 12-volt battery wait two minutes before proceeding, remove the ORC fuses, connect the 12-volt battery, wait two minutes before proceeding. Cycle the ignition to the On position, then reconnect the ORC fuses. Wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">fatal injury.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Measure the voltage of the (R79) Front Left Impact Sensor Signal circuit and (R81) Sensor Ground circuit at the Front Left Impact Sensor harness connector and ground.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Is there any voltage present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (R79, R81) Front Left Impact Sensor circuits for a short to voltage.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (R79) FRONT LEFT IMPACT SENSOR SIGNAL CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO GROUND</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:      Turn the ignition off disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (R79) Front Left Impact Sensor Signal circuit between the Front Left</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Impact Sensor harness connector and ground.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Is the resistance below 100K Ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (R79) Front Left Impact Sensor Signal circuit for a short to ground.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Go To 4</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK THE (R79, R81) FRONT LEFT IMPACT SENSOR CIRCUITS FOR A SHORT TOGETHER</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Measure the resistance between the (R79) Front Left Impact Sensor Signal and (R81) Sensor Ground circuits at the Front Left Impact Sensor harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Is the resistance below 100K Ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (R79, R81) Front Left Impact Sensor circuits shorted together.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Go To 5</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>CHECK THE (R81) FRONT LEFT IMPACT SENSOR GROUND CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN OR HIGH RESISTANCE</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:       Turn the ignition off, disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the ORC module and the ORC Module body harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Connect the test leads to the DVOM.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (R81) Front Left Impact Sensor Ground circuit between the Front Left Impact Sensor connector terminal 2 and the ORC Module body harness connector terminal C1-14.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance below 1 Ohm?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 6</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (R81) Front Left Impact Sensor Ground circuit for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>CHECK THE (R79) FRONT LEFT IMPACT SENSOR CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN OR HIGH RESISTANCE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (R79) Front Left Impact Sensor Ground circuit between the Front Left Impact Sensor connector terminal 1 and the ORC Module body harness connector terminal C1-13.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance below 1 Ohm?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 7</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (R79) Front Left Impact Sensor Signal circuit for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>CHECK OPERATION OF THE FRONT LEFT IMPACT SENSOR</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Replace the Front Left Impact Sensor in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to SENSOR, IMPACT, REMOVAL .</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Reconnect the vehicle body harness to the impact sensor.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Remove any special tools or jumper wires and reconnect all previously disconnected components - except the Battery.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the standard key ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition on, then reconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the keyless ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Disconnect the 12-volt battery wait two minutes before proceeding, remove the ORC fuses, connect the 12-volt battery, wait two minutes before proceeding. Cycle the ignition to the On position, then reconnect the ORC fuses. Wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Connect the scan tool to the Data Link Connector - use the most current software available.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Use the scan tool and erase the stored codes in all airbag system modules.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>Turn the Ignition Off, and wait 15 seconds before turning the Ignition On.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>Wait one minute, and read active codes and if there are none present read the stored codes.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Did the active Front Left Impact Sensor DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 8</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Repair is complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>CHECK RELATED HARNESS CONNECTIONS</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:       Turn the ignition off, disconnect the battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:       If the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) is dropped at any time, it must be replaced. Failure to take the proper precautions could result in accidental airbag deployment. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect all Occupant Restraint Controller(ORC) harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect all related in-line harness connections (if equipped).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Disconnect the related component harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Inspect harness connectors, component connectors, and all male and female terminals for the following conditions:</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Proper connector installation. Damaged connector locks. Corrosion. Other signs of water intrusion. Weather seal damage (if equipped). Bent terminals. Overheating due to a poor connection (terminal may be discolored due to excessive current draw). Terminals that have been pushed back into the connector cavity. Check for spread terminals and verify proper terminal tension.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Repair any conditions that are found.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Connect all Occupant Restraint Controller(ORC) harness connectors. Be certain that all harness connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Connect all in-line harness connectors (if equipped). Be certain that all connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Connect all related component harness connectors. Be certain that all connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>Test drive or operate the vehicle in accordance with the when monitored and set conditions.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">10</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Replace and program the Occupant Restraint Controller in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">The wiring or poor connection problem has been repaired.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the Occupant Restraint Controller VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b0090-13 left frontal acceleration sensor circuit open\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B0090-13</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">LEFT FRONTAL ACCELERATION SENSOR CIRCUIT OPEN</small><small>العطل: دائرة مفتوحة</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">When powered, the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) sends a test current to the Impact/Pressure Sensors to verify the integrity of the sensor and wiring.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">With the ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">When powered, the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) sends a test current to the Impact/Pressure Sensors to verify the integrity of the sensor and wiring.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This DTC may inhibit deployment or modify deployment strategy.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>LEFT FRONT IMPACT SENSOR SIGNAL CIRCUITS OPEN</li><li>LEFT FRONT IMPACT SENSOR CIRCUITS SHORTED TO VOLTAGE</li><li>LEFT FRONT IMPACT SENSOR</li><li>OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER (ORC)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM PRE-DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read ORC DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Record the Environmental Data.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using the recorded Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read ORC DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM INTERMITTENT TEST . Probing of the circuit cavities at the ORC Module body harness connectors or vehicle connectors is only to be done with a approved test lead from the test lead 10159-6 or the use of Breakout Box 8443-55 to prevent vehicle wiring harness connector damage during diagnostic procedures.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE (R79, R81) FRONT LEFT IMPACT SENSOR SIGNAL AND GROUND CIRCUITS FOR A SHORT CIRCUITS</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:      Turn the ignition off, disconnect the battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the Front Left Impact Sensor harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the ORC Module harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the standard key ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition on, then reconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the keyless ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Disconnect the 12-volt battery wait two minutes before proceeding, remove the ORC fuses, connect the 12-volt battery, wait two minutes before proceeding. Cycle the ignition to the On position, then reconnect the ORC fuses. Wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">fatal injury.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Measure the voltage of the (R79) Front Left Impact Sensor Signal circuit and (R81) Sensor Ground circuit at the Front Left Impact Sensor harness connector and ground.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Is there any voltage present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (R79, R81) Front Left Impact Sensor circuits for a short to voltage.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (R79) FRONT LEFT IMPACT SENSOR SIGNAL CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO GROUND</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:      Turn the ignition off disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (R79) Front Left Impact Sensor Signal circuit between the Front Left</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Impact Sensor harness connector and ground.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Is the resistance below 100K Ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (R79) Front Left Impact Sensor Signal circuit for a short to ground.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Go To 4</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK THE (R79, R81) FRONT LEFT IMPACT SENSOR CIRCUITS FOR A SHORT TOGETHER</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Measure the resistance between the (R79) Front Left Impact Sensor Signal and (R81) Sensor Ground circuits at the Front Left Impact Sensor harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Is the resistance below 100K Ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (R79, R81) Front Left Impact Sensor circuits shorted together.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Go To 5</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>CHECK THE (R81) FRONT LEFT IMPACT SENSOR GROUND CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN OR HIGH RESISTANCE</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:       Turn the ignition off, disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the ORC module and the ORC Module body harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Connect the test leads to the DVOM.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (R81) Front Left Impact Sensor Ground circuit between the Front Left Impact Sensor connector terminal 2 and the ORC Module body harness connector terminal C1-14.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance below 1 Ohm?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 6</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (R81) Front Left Impact Sensor Ground circuit for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>CHECK THE (R79) FRONT LEFT IMPACT SENSOR CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN OR HIGH RESISTANCE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (R79) Front Left Impact Sensor Ground circuit between the Front Left Impact Sensor connector terminal 1 and the ORC Module body harness connector terminal C1-13.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance below 1 Ohm?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 7</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (R79) Front Left Impact Sensor Signal circuit for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>CHECK OPERATION OF THE FRONT LEFT IMPACT SENSOR</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Replace the Front Left Impact Sensor in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to SENSOR, IMPACT, REMOVAL .</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Reconnect the vehicle body harness to the impact sensor.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Remove any special tools or jumper wires and reconnect all previously disconnected components - except the Battery.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the standard key ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition on, then reconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the keyless ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Disconnect the 12-volt battery wait two minutes before proceeding, remove the ORC fuses, connect the 12-volt battery, wait two minutes before proceeding. Cycle the ignition to the On position, then reconnect the ORC fuses. Wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Connect the scan tool to the Data Link Connector - use the most current software available.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Use the scan tool and erase the stored codes in all airbag system modules.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>Turn the Ignition Off, and wait 15 seconds before turning the Ignition On.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>Wait one minute, and read active codes and if there are none present read the stored codes.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Did the active Front Left Impact Sensor DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 8</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Repair is complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>REPLACE THE OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER (ORC)</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:       Turn the ignition off disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:       If the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) is dropped at any time, it must be replaced. Failure to take the proper precautions could result in accidental airbag deployment. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Repair</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Replace the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) in accordance with Service Information. Refer to MODULE, OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b0090-49 left frontal impact sensor internal electronic failure\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B0090-49</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">LEFT FRONTAL IMPACT SENSOR INTERNAL ELECTRONIC FAILURE</small><small>العطل: عطل إلكتروني داخلي</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Impact sensors perform internal self-tests and communicate the sensors status using power supplied by the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC). The sensor communicates this internal failure message using the sensor signal circuit. If the scan tool shows this DTC has a Stored history of setting then the left front impact sensor is to be replaced.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">With the ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This DTC sets when the ORC receives notification of a self-test failure within the impact sensor. Once set, this DTC is latched for the entire ignition cycle.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This DTC may inhibit deployment or modify deployment strategy.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>LEFT FRONT IMPACT SENSOR</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM PRE-DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">VERIFY ACTIVE DTC</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           If the scan tool shows this DTC has a Stored history of setting then the right front impact sensor is to be replaced.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Make sure the battery is fully charged.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read ORC DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Does the scan tool display an active B0095-49-RIGHT FRONTAL ACCELERATION SENSOR - INTERNAL ELECTRONIC FAILURE DTC or shows a setting history in stored?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Right Front Impact Sensor in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to SENSOR, IMPACT, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINT SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to STANDARD PROCEDURE .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">No (Did not set a active or stored DTC B0095-49- RIGHT FRONTAL SENSOR - INTERNAL ELECTRONIC FAILURE)</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM INTERMITTENT TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b0090-87 left frontal impact sensor missing message\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B0090-87</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">LEFT FRONTAL IMPACT SENSOR MISSING MESSAGE</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The impact sensors perform their own self test using power supplied by the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) then communicate this status back to the ORC with periodic updates. The repair of this fault condition involves verifying the integrity of the wiring between the ORC and the sensor.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">With the ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This DTC sets when the ORC does not receive a message from the sensor. Once set, this DTC is latched for the entire ignition cycle.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This DTC may inhibit deployment or modify deployment strategy.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>SIGNAL CIRCUITS SHORTED TO VOLTAGE OR GROUND</li><li>FRONT LEFT IMPACT SENSOR CIRCUITS SHORTED TOGETHER</li><li>FRONT LEFT IMPACT SENSOR</li><li>OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER (ORC)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM PRE-DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read ORC DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Record the Environmental Data.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using the recorded Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read ORC DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM INTERMITTENT TEST . Probing of the circuit cavities at the ORC Module body harness connectors or vehicle connectors is only to be done with a approved test lead from the test lead 10159-6 or the use of Breakout Box 8443-55 to prevent vehicle wiring harness connector damage during diagnostic procedures.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE (R79, R81) FRONT LEFT IMPACT SENSOR SIGNAL AND GROUND CIRCUITS FOR A SHORT CIRCUITS</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:      Turn the ignition off, disconnect the battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the Front Left Impact Sensor harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the ORC Module harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the standard key ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition on, then reconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the keyless ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Disconnect the 12-volt battery wait two minutes before proceeding, remove the ORC fuses, connect the 12-volt battery, wait two minutes before proceeding. Cycle the ignition to the On position, then reconnect the ORC fuses. Wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">fatal injury.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Measure the voltage of the (R79) Front Left Impact Sensor Signal circuit and (R81) Sensor Ground circuit at the Front Left Impact Sensor harness connector and ground.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Is there any voltage present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (R79, R81) Front Left Impact Sensor circuits for a short to voltage.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (R79) FRONT LEFT IMPACT SENSOR SIGNAL CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO GROUND</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:      Turn the ignition off disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (R79) Front Left Impact Sensor Signal circuit between the Front Left</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Impact Sensor harness connector and ground.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Is the resistance below 100K Ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (R79) Front Left Impact Sensor Signal circuit for a short to ground.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Go To 4</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK THE (R79, R81) FRONT LEFT IMPACT SENSOR CIRCUITS FOR A SHORT TOGETHER</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Measure the resistance between the (R79) Front Left Impact Sensor Signal and (R81) Sensor Ground circuits at the Front Left Impact Sensor harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Is the resistance below 100K Ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (R79, R81) Front Left Impact Sensor circuits shorted together.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Go To 5</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>CHECK THE (R81) FRONT LEFT IMPACT SENSOR GROUND CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN OR HIGH RESISTANCE</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:       Turn the ignition off, disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the ORC module and the ORC Module body harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Connect the test leads to the DVOM.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (R81) Front Left Impact Sensor Ground circuit between the Front Left Impact Sensor connector terminal 2 and the ORC Module body harness connector terminal C1-14.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance below 1 Ohm?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 6</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (R81) Front Left Impact Sensor Ground circuit for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>CHECK THE (R79) FRONT LEFT IMPACT SENSOR CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN OR HIGH RESISTANCE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (R79) Front Left Impact Sensor Ground circuit between the Front Left Impact Sensor connector terminal 1 and the ORC Module body harness connector terminal C1-13.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance below 1 Ohm?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 7</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (R79) Front Left Impact Sensor Signal circuit for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>CHECK OPERATION OF THE FRONT LEFT IMPACT SENSOR</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Replace the Front Left Impact Sensor in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to SENSOR, IMPACT, REMOVAL .</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Reconnect the vehicle body harness to the impact sensor.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Remove any special tools or jumper wires and reconnect all previously disconnected components - except the Battery.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the standard key ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition on, then reconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the keyless ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Disconnect the 12-volt battery wait two minutes before proceeding, remove the ORC fuses, connect the 12-volt battery, wait two minutes before proceeding. Cycle the ignition to the On position, then reconnect the ORC fuses. Wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Connect the scan tool to the Data Link Connector - use the most current software available.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Use the scan tool and erase the stored codes in all airbag system modules.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>Turn the Ignition Off, and wait 15 seconds before turning the Ignition On.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>Wait one minute, and read active codes and if there are none present read the stored codes.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Did the active Front Left Impact Sensor DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 8</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Repair is complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>CHECK RELATED HARNESS CONNECTIONS</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:       Turn the ignition off, disconnect the battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:       If the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) is dropped at any time, it must be replaced. Failure to take the proper precautions could result in accidental airbag deployment. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect all Occupant Restraint Controller(ORC) harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect all related in-line harness connections (if equipped).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Disconnect the related component harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Inspect harness connectors, component connectors, and all male and female terminals for the following conditions:</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Proper connector installation. Damaged connector locks. Corrosion. Other signs of water intrusion. Weather seal damage (if equipped). Bent terminals. Overheating due to a poor connection (terminal may be discolored due to excessive current draw). Terminals that have been pushed back into the connector cavity. Check for spread terminals and verify proper terminal tension.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Repair any conditions that are found.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Connect all Occupant Restraint Controller(ORC) harness connectors. Be certain that all harness connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Connect all in-line harness connectors (if equipped). Be certain that all connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Connect all related component harness connectors. Be certain that all connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>Test drive or operate the vehicle in accordance with the when monitored and set conditions.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">10</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Replace and program the Occupant Restraint Controller in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">The wiring or poor connection problem has been repaired.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the Occupant Restraint Controller VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b0090-95 left frontal impact sensor incorrect assembly\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B0090-95</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">LEFT FRONTAL IMPACT SENSOR INCORRECT ASSEMBLY</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">When powered, the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) sends a test current to the impact sensors. During this test, the sensors discovered are checked for agreement with the pre-programmed configuration of components assigned to the module. The repair of this fault condition centers on confirming the correct module and wiring is installed in the vehicle.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs once during the initialization process.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">With the ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This DTC sets when the ORC detects the presence of an Impact Sensor circuit while the configuration of the module does not reflect a n Impact Sensor should be present. Once set, this DTC is latched for the entire power cycle and requires the module to be re-initalized to set code.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This DTC may inhibit deployment or modify deployment strategy.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>UNUSED IMPACT SENSOR CIRCUITS SHORTED TO VOLTAGE, SHORTED TO GROUND, OR</li><li>SHORTED TOGETHER</li><li>OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER (ORC)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM PRE-DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">DETERMINE ACTIVE OR STORED DTC</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Make sure the battery is fully charged.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Perform ORC module reset. Access the Miscellaneous Function menu from the ORC ECU Overview screen on the scan tool to perform this operation.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, read ORC DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Is the DTC active or stored?</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">ORC - ACTIVE DTC</p><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition off disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Inspect the related wiring harness for chafed, pierced, pinched, and partially broken wires. Also, inspect the related connectors for broken, bent, pushed out, spread, corroded, or contaminated terminals. Repair as necessary. If no short or damage is found, replace the ORC in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER, REMOVAL .</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Make sure the part number of the replacement module is the correct part number for the vehicle.</div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        If the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) is dropped at any time, it must be replaced. Failure to take the proper precautions can result in accidental airbag deployment. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to STANDARD PROCEDURE</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">ORC - STORED DTC</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM INTERMITTENT TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b0090-9a left frontal impact sensor component or system operating\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B0090-9A</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">LEFT FRONTAL IMPACT SENSOR COMPONENT OR SYSTEM OPERATING</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">CONDITIONS</p></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">When powered, the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) sends a test current to the left front impact sensor to verify the integrity of the sensor and wiring. The presence of this code indicates that any two circuits, from two or more impact sensors, have become shorted or &quot;coupled&quot; together.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The ORC checks the Impact Sensor circuits once during the initialization process.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Module detects that two Impact Sensor lines from separate circuits are coupled together.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Once set, the DTC is latched for the entire power cycle and requires the module to be re-initialized to transition code from active to stored. This DTC may inhibit deployment or modify deployment strategy.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>2 IMPACT SENSOR LINES FROM SEPARATE CIRCUITS COUPLED TOGETHER</li><li>OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER (ORC)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM PRE-DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>DETERMINE ACTIVE OR STORED DTC</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Make sure the battery is fully charged.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Perform ORC module reset. Access the Miscellaneous Function menu from the ORC ECU Overview screen on the scan tool to perform this operation.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Using the scan tool, read ORC DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active or stored?</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">ORC - ACTIVE DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLE CODE (DTC)</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">ORC - STORED DTC</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM INTERMITTENT TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK FOR ADDITIONAL ACTIVE SQUIB DTCS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Using the scan tool, read ORC DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are there sensor specific DTCs set as active in addition to B0090-9A-LEFT FRONTAL RESTRAINTS SENSOR - COMPONENT OR SYSTEM OPERATING CONDITIONS?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair all other active sensor specific DTCs before repairing B0090-9A-LEFT FRONTAL RESTRAINTS SENSOR - COMPONENT OR SYSTEM OPERATING CONDITIONS.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>USE THE SCAN TOOL TO IDENTIFY THE COUPLED CIRCUITS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Using the scan tool, identify the two or more sensor circuits that read SET.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are two or more sensor circuits DTCs set?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the two or more sensor circuits for a Sensor Circuit Coupling condition.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM INTERMITTENT TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b0095-11 right frontal acceleration sensor circuit short to ground\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B0095-11</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">RIGHT FRONTAL ACCELERATION SENSOR CIRCUIT SHORT TO GROUND</small><small>العطل: قصر على الأرضي</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">When powered, the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) sends a test current to the Impact/Pressure Sensors to verify the integrity of the sensor and wiring.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) monitors the Impact/Pressure Sensor circuits for multiple circuit failures. If the controller detects a circuit value that is out of the allowable range, the ORC will set this DTC.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This DTC may or may not allow the squib to deploy during a crash event.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>RIGHT FRONT IMPACT SENSOR SIGNAL CIRCUITS SHORTED TO GROUND</li><li>RIGHT FRONT IMPACT SENSOR CIRCUITS SHORTED TOGETHER</li><li>RIGHT FRONT IMPACT SENSOR</li><li>OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER (ORC)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM PRE-DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read ORC DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Record the Environmental Data.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using the recorded Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read ORC DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM INTERMITTENT TEST . Probing of the circuit cavities at the ORC Module body harness connectors or vehicle connectors is only to be done with a approved test lead from the test lead 10159-6 or the use of Breakout Box 8443-55 to prevent vehicle wiring harness connector damage during diagnostic procedures.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE (R80, R82) FRONT RIGHT IMPACT SENSOR SIGNAL AND GROUND CIRCUITS FOR A SHORT TO GROUND</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:      Turn the ignition off disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the Right Front Impact Sensor harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the ORC harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the standard key ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition on, then reconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the keyless ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Disconnect the 12-volt battery wait two minutes before proceeding, remove the ORC fuses, connect the 12-volt battery, wait two minutes before proceeding. Cycle the ignition to the On position, then reconnect the ORC fuses. Wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Measure the voltage of the (R80) Front Right Impact Sensor Signal circuit and (R82) Sensor Ground circuit at the Front Right Impact Sensor connector and ground.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Is there any voltage present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (R80 and R82) Front Right Impact Sensor circuits for a short to voltage.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (R80, 82) FRONT RIGHT IMPACT SENSOR SIGNAL CIRCUITS FOR A SHORT TO GROUND</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the standard key ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition on, then reconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the keyless ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Disconnect the 12-volt battery wait two minutes before proceeding, remove the ORC fuses, connect the 12-volt battery, wait two minutes before proceeding. Cycle the ignition to the On position, then reconnect the ORC fuses. Wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (R80, R82) Front Right Impact Sensor Signal circuitS between the Front Right Impact Sensor connector and ground.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Is the resistance below 100K ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (R80, R82) Front Right Impact Sensor Signal circuits for a short to ground.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Go To 4</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK THE (R80, R82) FRONT RIGHT IMPACT SENSOR CIRCUITS FOR A SHORT TOGETHER</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Measure the resistance between the (R80) Front Right Impact Sensor Signal and (R82) Sensor Ground circuits at the Front Right Impact Sensor harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Is the resistance below 100K Ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (R80, R82) Front Right Impact Sensor circuits shorted together.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 5</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>CHECK THE (R82) FRONT RIGHT IMPACT SENSOR GROUND CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN OR HIGH RESISTANCE</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:       Turn the ignition off, disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the ORC module and the ORC Module body harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Connect the test leads to the DVOM.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (R82) Front Right Impact Sensor Ground circuit between the Front Right Impact Sensor connector terminal 2 and the ORC Module body harness connector terminal C2-85.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance below 1 Ohm?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 6</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (R82) Front Right Impact Sensor Ground circuit for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>CHECK THE (R80) FRONT RIGHT IMPACT SENSOR CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN OR HIGH RESISTANCE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (R80) Front Right Impact Sensor Signal circuit between the Front Right Impact Sensor connector terminal 1 and the ORC Module body harness connector terminal C-86.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance below 1 Ohm?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 7</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (R80) Front Right Impact Sensor Signal circuit for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>CHECK OPERATION OF THE FRONT RIGHT IMPACT SENSOR</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Replace the Front Right Impact Sensor in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to SENSOR, IMPACT, REMOVAL .</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Reconnect the vehicle body harness to the impact sensor.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Remove any special tools or jumper wires and reconnect all previously disconnected components - except the Battery.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the standard key ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition on, then reconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the keyless ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Disconnect the 12-volt battery wait two minutes before proceeding, remove the ORC fuses, connect the 12-volt battery, wait two minutes before proceeding. Cycle the ignition to the On position, then reconnect the ORC fuses. Wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Connect the scan tool to the Data Link Connector - use the most current software available.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Use the scan tool and erase the stored codes in all airbag system modules.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>Turn the Ignition Off, and wait 15 seconds before turning the Ignition On.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>Wait one minute, and read active codes and if there are none present read the stored codes.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Did the active Front Right Impact Sensor DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 8</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Repair is complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>REPLACE THE OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER (ORC)</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition off disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        If the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) is dropped at any time, it must be replaced. Failure to take the proper precautions could result in accidental airbag deployment. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">If there are no possible causes remaining, view repair.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Repair</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Replace the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) in accordance with Service Information. Refer to MODULE, OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b0095-12 right frontal acceleration sensor circuit short to battery\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B0095-12</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">RIGHT FRONTAL ACCELERATION SENSOR CIRCUIT SHORT TO BATTERY</small><small>العطل: قصر على البطارية</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">When powered, the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) sends a test current to the Impact/Pressure Sensors to verify the integrity of the sensor and wiring.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) monitors the Impact/Pressure Sensor circuits for multiple circuit failures. If the controller detects a circuit value that is out of the allowable range, the ORC will set this DTC.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This DTC may or may not allow the squib to deploy during a crash event.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>RIGHT FRONT IMPACT SENSOR SIGNAL CIRCUITS SHORTED TO VOLTAGE</li><li>RIGHT FRONT IMPACT SENSOR CIRCUITS SHORTED TOGETHER</li><li>RIGHT FRONT IMPACT SENSOR</li><li>OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER (ORC)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM PRE-DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read ORC DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Record the Environmental Data.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using the recorded Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read ORC DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM INTERMITTENT TEST . Probing of the circuit cavities at the ORC Module body harness connectors or vehicle connectors is only to be done with a approved test lead from the test lead 10159-6 or the use of Breakout Box 8443-55 to prevent vehicle wiring harness connector damage during diagnostic procedures.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE (R80, R82) FRONT RIGHT IMPACT SENSOR SIGNAL AND GROUND CIRCUITS FOR A SHORT TO VOLTAGE</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:      Turn the ignition off disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the Right Front Impact Sensor harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the ORC harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the standard key ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition on, then reconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the keyless ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Disconnect the 12-volt battery wait two minutes before proceeding, remove the ORC fuses, connect the 12-volt battery, wait two minutes before proceeding. Cycle the ignition to the On position, then reconnect the ORC fuses. Wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Measure the voltage of the (R80) Front Right Impact Sensor Signal circuit and (R82) Sensor Ground circuit at the Front Right Impact Sensor connector and ground.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Is there any voltage present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (R80 and R82) Front Right Impact Sensor circuits for a short to voltage.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (R80, 82) FRONT RIGHT IMPACT SENSOR SIGNAL CIRCUITS FOR A SHORT TO GROUND</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the standard key ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition on, then reconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the keyless ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Disconnect the 12-volt battery wait two minutes before proceeding, remove the ORC fuses, connect the 12-volt battery, wait two minutes before proceeding. Cycle the ignition to the On position, then reconnect the ORC fuses. Wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (R80, R82) Front Right Impact Sensor Signal circuitS between the Front Right Impact Sensor connector and ground.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Is the resistance below 100K ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (R80, R82) Front Right Impact Sensor Signal circuits for a short to ground.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Go To 4</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK THE (R80, R82) FRONT RIGHT IMPACT SENSOR CIRCUITS FOR A SHORT TOGETHER</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Measure the resistance between the (R80) Front Right Impact Sensor Signal and (R82) Sensor Ground circuits at the Front Right Impact Sensor harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Is the resistance below 100K Ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (R80, R82) Front Right Impact Sensor circuits shorted together.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 5</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>CHECK THE (R82) FRONT RIGHT IMPACT SENSOR GROUND CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN OR HIGH RESISTANCE</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:       Turn the ignition off, disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the ORC module and the ORC Module body harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Connect the test leads to the DVOM.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (R82) Front Right Impact Sensor Ground circuit between the Front Right Impact Sensor connector terminal 2 and the ORC Module body harness connector terminal C2-85.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance below 1 Ohm?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 6</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (R82) Front Right Impact Sensor Ground circuit for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>CHECK THE (R80) FRONT RIGHT IMPACT SENSOR CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN OR HIGH RESISTANCE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (R80) Front Right Impact Sensor Signal circuit between the Front Right Impact Sensor connector terminal 1 and the ORC Module body harness connector terminal C2-86.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance below 1 Ohm?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 7</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (R80) Front Right Impact Sensor Signal circuit for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>CHECK OPERATION OF THE FRONT RIGHT IMPACT SENSOR</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Replace the Front Right Impact Sensor in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to SENSOR, IMPACT, REMOVAL .</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Reconnect the vehicle body harness to the impact sensor.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Remove any special tools or jumper wires and reconnect all previously disconnected components - except the Battery.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the standard key ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition on, then reconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the keyless ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Disconnect the 12-volt battery wait two minutes before proceeding, remove the ORC fuses, connect the 12-volt battery, wait two minutes before proceeding. Cycle the ignition to the On position, then reconnect the ORC fuses. Wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Connect the scan tool to the Data Link Connector - use the most current software available.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Use the scan tool and erase the stored codes in all airbag system modules.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>Turn the Ignition Off, and wait 15 seconds before turning the Ignition On.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>Wait one minute, and read active codes and if there are none present read the stored codes.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Did the active Front Right Impact Sensor DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 8</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Repair is complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>REPLACE THE OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER (ORC)</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition off disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        If the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) is dropped at any time, it must be replaced. Failure to take the proper precautions could result in accidental airbag deployment. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">If there are no possible causes remaining, view repair.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Repair</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Replace the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) in accordance with Service Information. Refer to MODULE, OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b0095-13 right frontal acceleration sensor circuit open\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B0095-13</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">RIGHT FRONTAL ACCELERATION SENSOR CIRCUIT OPEN</small><small>العطل: دائرة مفتوحة</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">When powered, the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) sends a test current to the Impact/Pressure Sensors to verify the integrity of the sensor and wiring.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">With the ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">When powered, the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) sends a test current to the Impact/Pressure Sensors to verify the integrity of the sensor and wiring.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This DTC may inhibit deployment or modify deployment strategy.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>RIGHT FRONT IMPACT SENSOR SIGNAL CIRCUITS OPEN</li><li>RIGHT FRONT IMPACT SENSOR CIRCUITS SHORTED TO VOLTAGE</li><li>RIGHT FRONT IMPACT SENSOR</li><li>OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER (ORC)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM PRE-DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read ORC DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Record the Environmental Data.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using the recorded Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read ORC DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM INTERMITTENT TEST . Probing of the circuit cavities at the ORC Module body harness connectors or vehicle connectors is only to be done with a approved test lead from the test lead 10159-6 or the use of Breakout Box 8443-55 to prevent vehicle wiring harness connector damage during diagnostic procedures.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE (R80, R82) FRONT RIGHT IMPACT SENSOR SIGNAL AND GROUND CIRCUITS FOR A SHORT TO VOLTAGE</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:      Turn the ignition off disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the Right Front Impact Sensor harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the ORC harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the standard key ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition on, then reconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the keyless ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Disconnect the 12-volt battery wait two minutes before proceeding, remove the ORC fuses, connect the 12-volt battery, wait two minutes before proceeding. Cycle the ignition to the On position, then reconnect the ORC fuses. Wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Measure the voltage of the (R80) Front Right Impact Sensor Signal circuit and (R82) Sensor Ground circuit at the Front Right Impact Sensor connector and ground.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Is there any voltage present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (R80 and R82) Front Right Impact Sensor circuits for a short to voltage.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (R80, 82) FRONT RIGHT IMPACT SENSOR SIGNAL CIRCUITS FOR A SHORT TO GROUND</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the standard key ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition on, then reconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the keyless ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Disconnect the 12-volt battery wait two minutes before proceeding, remove the ORC fuses, connect the 12-volt battery, wait two minutes before proceeding. Cycle the ignition to the On position, then reconnect the ORC fuses. Wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (R80, R82) Front Right Impact Sensor Signal circuitS between the Front Right Impact Sensor connector and ground.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Is the resistance below 100K ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (R80, R82) Front Right Impact Sensor Signal circuits for a short to ground.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Go To 4</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK THE (R80, R82) FRONT RIGHT IMPACT SENSOR CIRCUITS FOR A SHORT TOGETHER</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Measure the resistance between the (R80) Front Right Impact Sensor Signal and (R82) Sensor Ground circuits at the Front Right Impact Sensor harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Is the resistance below 100K Ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (R80, R82) Front Right Impact Sensor circuits shorted together.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 5</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>CHECK THE (R82) FRONT RIGHT IMPACT SENSOR GROUND CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN OR HIGH RESISTANCE</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:       Turn the ignition off, disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the ORC module and the ORC Module body harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Connect the test leads to the DVOM.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (R82) Front Right Impact Sensor Ground circuit between the Front Right Impact Sensor connector terminal 2 and the ORC Module body harness connector terminal C2-85.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance below 1 Ohm?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 6</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (R82) Front Right Impact Sensor Ground circuit for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>CHECK THE (R80) FRONT RIGHT IMPACT SENSOR CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN OR HIGH RESISTANCE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (R80) Front Right Impact Sensor Signal circuit between the Front Right Impact Sensor connector terminal 1 and the ORC Module body harness connector terminal C2-86.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance below 1 Ohm?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 7</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (R80) Front Right Impact Sensor Signal circuit for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>CHECK OPERATION OF THE FRONT RIGHT IMPACT SENSOR</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Replace the Front Right Impact Sensor in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to SENSOR, IMPACT, REMOVAL .</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Reconnect the vehicle body harness to the impact sensor.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Remove any special tools or jumper wires and reconnect all previously disconnected components - except the Battery.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the standard key ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition on, then reconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the keyless ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Disconnect the 12-volt battery wait two minutes before proceeding, remove the ORC fuses, connect the 12-volt battery, wait two minutes before proceeding. Cycle the ignition to the On position, then reconnect the ORC fuses. Wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Connect the scan tool to the Data Link Connector - use the most current software available.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Use the scan tool and erase the stored codes in all airbag system modules.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>Turn the Ignition Off, and wait 15 seconds before turning the Ignition On.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>Wait one minute, and read active codes and if there are none present read the stored codes.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Did the active Front Right Impact Sensor DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 8</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Repair is complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>REPLACE THE OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER (ORC)</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition off disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        If the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) is dropped at any time, it must be replaced. Failure to take the proper precautions could result in accidental airbag deployment. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">If there are no possible causes remaining, view repair.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Repair</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Replace the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) in accordance with Service Information. Refer to MODULE, OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b0095-49 right frontal acceleration sensor internal electronic failure\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B0095-49</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">RIGHT FRONTAL ACCELERATION SENSOR INTERNAL ELECTRONIC FAILURE</small><small>العطل: عطل إلكتروني داخلي</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Impact sensors perform internal self-tests and communicate the sensors status using power supplied by the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC). The sensor communicates this internal failure message using the sensor signal circuit. If the scan tool shows this DTC has a Stored history of setting then the right front impact sensor is to be replaced.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">With the ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This DTC sets when the ORC receives notification of a self-test failure within the impact sensor. Once set, this DTC is latched for the entire ignition cycle.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This DTC may inhibit deployment or modify deployment strategy.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>RIGHT FRONT IMPACT SENSOR</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM PRE-DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">VERIFY ACTIVE DTC</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           If the scan tool shows this DTC has a Stored history of setting then the right front impact sensor is to be replaced.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Make sure the battery is fully charged.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read ORC DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Does the scan tool display an active B0095-49-RIGHT FRONTAL ACCELERATION SENSOR - INTERNAL ELECTRONIC FAILURE DTC or shows a setting history in stored?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Right Front Impact Sensor in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to SENSOR, IMPACT, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINT SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to STANDARD PROCEDURE .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">No (Did not set a active or stored DTC B0095-49- RIGHT FRONTAL SENSOR - INTERNAL ELECTRONIC FAILURE)</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM INTERMITTENT TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b0095-87 right frontal impact sensor missing message\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B0095-87</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">RIGHT FRONTAL IMPACT SENSOR MISSING MESSAGE</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The impact sensors perform their own self test using power supplied by the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) then communicate this status back to the ORC with periodic updates. The repair of this fault condition involves verifying the integrity of the wiring between the ORC and the sensor.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">With the ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This DTC sets when the ORC does not receive a message from the sensor. Once set, this DTC is latched for the entire ignition cycle.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This DTC may inhibit deployment or modify deployment strategy.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>SIGNAL CIRCUITS SHORTED TO VOLTAGE OR GROUND</li><li>FRONT RIGHT IMPACT SENSOR CIRCUITS SHORTED TOGETHER</li><li>RIGHT FRONT IMPACT SENSOR</li><li>OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER (ORC)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM PRE-DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read ORC DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Record the Environmental Data.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using the recorded Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read ORC DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM INTERMITTENT TEST . Probing of the circuit cavities at the ORC Module body harness connectors or vehicle connectors is only to be done with a approved test lead from the test lead 10159-6 or the use of Breakout Box 8443-55 to prevent vehicle wiring harness connector damage during diagnostic procedures.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE (R80, R82) FRONT RIGHT IMPACT SENSOR SIGNAL AND GROUND</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">CIRCUITS FOR A SHORT TO VOLTAGE</p><pre class=\"en-pre\">          WARNING:        Turn the ignition off disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two\n                          minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may\n     1.                   result in possible serious or fatal injury.</pre><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Right Front Impact Sensor harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Disconnect the ORC harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the standard key ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition on, then reconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the keyless ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Disconnect the 12-volt battery wait two minutes before proceeding, remove the ORC fuses, connect the 12-volt battery, wait two minutes before proceeding. Cycle the ignition to the On position, then reconnect the ORC fuses. Wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Measure the voltage of the (R80) Front Right Impact Sensor Signal circuit and (R82) Sensor Ground circuit at the Front Right Impact Sensor connector and ground.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there any voltage present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Repair the (R80 and R82) Front Right Impact Sensor circuits for a short to voltage.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (R80, 82) FRONT RIGHT IMPACT SENSOR SIGNAL CIRCUITS FOR A SHORT TO GROUND</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the standard key ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition on, then reconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the keyless ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Disconnect the 12-volt battery wait two minutes before proceeding, remove the ORC fuses, connect the 12-volt battery, wait two minutes before proceeding. Cycle the ignition to the On position, then</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">reconnect the ORC fuses. Wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (R80, R82) Front Right Impact Sensor Signal circuitS between the Front Right Impact Sensor connector and ground.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Is the resistance below 100K ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (R80, R82) Front Right Impact Sensor Signal circuits for a short to ground.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Go To 2</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK THE (R80, R82) FRONT RIGHT IMPACT SENSOR CIRCUITS FOR A SHORT TOGETHER</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Measure the resistance between the (R80) Front Right Impact Sensor Signal and (R82) Sensor Ground circuits at the Front Right Impact Sensor harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Is the resistance below 100K Ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (R80, R82) Front Right Impact Sensor circuits shorted together.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Go To 5</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>CHECK THE (R82) FRONT RIGHT IMPACT SENSOR GROUND CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN OR HIGH RESISTANCE</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:       Turn the ignition off, disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the ORC module and the ORC Module body harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Connect the test leads to the DVOM.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (R82) Front Right Impact Sensor Ground circuit between the Front Right Impact Sensor connector terminal 2 and the ORC Module body harness connector terminal C2-85.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance below 1 Ohm?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 6</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (R82) Front Right Impact Sensor Ground circuit for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>CHECK THE (R80) FRONT RIGHT IMPACT SENSOR CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN OR HIGH RESISTANCE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (R80) Front Right Impact Sensor Signal circuit between the Front Right Impact Sensor connector terminal 1 and the ORC Module body harness connector terminal C2-86.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance below 1 Ohm?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 7</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (R80) Front Right Impact Sensor Signal circuit for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>CHECK OPERATION OF THE FRONT RIGHT IMPACT SENSOR</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Replace the Front Right Impact Sensor in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">SENSOR, IMPACT, REMOVAL .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Reconnect the vehicle body harness to the impact sensor.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Remove any special tools or jumper wires and reconnect all previously disconnected components - except the Battery.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the standard key ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition on, then reconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the keyless ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Disconnect the 12-volt battery wait two minutes before proceeding, remove the ORC fuses, connect the 12-volt battery, wait two minutes before proceeding. Cycle the ignition to the On position, then reconnect the ORC fuses. Wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Connect the scan tool to the Data Link Connector - use the most current software available.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Use the scan tool and erase the stored codes in all airbag system modules.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>Turn the Ignition Off, and wait 15 seconds before turning the Ignition On.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>Wait one minute, and read active codes and if there are none present read the stored codes.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Did the active Front Right Impact Sensor DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 8</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Repair is complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>CHECK RELATED HARNESS CONNECTIONS</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:       Turn the ignition off, disconnect the battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:       If the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) is dropped at any time, it must be replaced. Failure to take the proper precautions could result in accidental airbag deployment. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect all Occupant Restraint Controller(ORC) harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect all related in-line harness connections (if equipped).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Disconnect the related component harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Inspect harness connectors, component connectors, and all male and female terminals for the following conditions: Proper connector installation. Damaged connector locks. Corrosion. Other signs of water intrusion. Weather seal damage (if equipped). Bent terminals. Overheating due to a poor connection (terminal may be discolored due to excessive current draw). Terminals that have been pushed back into the connector cavity. Check for spread terminals and verify proper terminal tension.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Repair any conditions that are found.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Connect all Occupant Restraint Controller(ORC) harness connectors. Be certain that all harness connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Connect all in-line harness connectors (if equipped). Be certain that all connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Connect all related component harness connectors. Be certain that all connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>Test drive or operate the vehicle in accordance with the when monitored and set conditions.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">10</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Replace and program the Occupant Restraint Controller in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">The wiring or poor connection problem has been repaired.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the Occupant Restraint Controller VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b0095-95 right frontal impact sensor incorrect assembly\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B0095-95</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">RIGHT FRONTAL IMPACT SENSOR INCORRECT ASSEMBLY</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">When powered, the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) sends a test current to the right front impact sensor. During this test, the impact sensors discovered are checked for agreement with the pre-programmed configuration of components assigned to the module. The repair of this fault condition centers on confirming the correct module and wiring is installed in the vehicle.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs once during the initialization process.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">With the ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This DTC sets when the ORC detects the presence of an Impact Sensor circuit while the configuration of the module does not reflect a n Impact Sensor should be present. Once set, this DTC is latched for the entire power cycle and requires the module to be re-initalized to set code.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This DTC may inhibit deployment or modify deployment strategy.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>UNUSED IMPACT SENSOR CIRCUITS SHORTED TO VOLTAGE, SHORTED TO GROUND, OR</li><li>SHORTED TOGETHER</li><li>OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER (ORC)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM PRE-DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR ACTIVE INTERNAL FAULTS, IGNITION FAULTS, AND BATTERY FAULTS IN THE OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER (ORC)</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:         Make sure the battery is fully charged.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Does the scan tool display any active DTCs relating to internal faults, ignition faults, or battery faults?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Diagnose and repair the DTCs. Refer to DIAGNOSTIC CODE INDEX .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>VERIFY THAT B0095-95-RIGHT FRONTAL ACCELERATION SENSOR - INCORRECT ASSEMBLY IS ACTIVE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, erase ORC DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Turn the ignition off, wait 10 seconds and then turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Wait 2 minutes, and then with the scan tool, read ORC DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Does the scan tool display active: B0095-95-RIGHT FRONTAL ACCELERATION SENSOR - INCORRECT ASSEMBLY?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>VERIFY WIRING</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Inspect the impact sensor wiring for a Right Front Impact Sensor.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Are Right Front Impact Sensor(s) present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition off, disconnect the battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        If the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) is dropped at any time, it must be replaced. Failure to take the proper precautions can result in accidental airbag deployment.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the ORC in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b0095-9a right frontal impact sensor component or system operating\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B0095-9A</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">RIGHT FRONTAL IMPACT SENSOR COMPONENT OR SYSTEM OPERATING</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">CONDITIONS</p></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">When powered, the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) sends a test current to the right front impact sensor to verify the integrity of the sensor and wiring. The presence of this code indicates that any two circuits, from two</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">or more impact sensors, have become shorted or &quot;coupled&quot; together.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The ORC checks the Impact Sensor circuits once during the initialization process.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Module detects that two Impact Sensor lines from separate circuits are coupled together.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Once set, the DTC is latched for the entire power cycle and requires the module to be re-initialized to transition code from active to stored. This DTC may inhibit deployment or modify deployment strategy.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>2 IMPACT SENSOR LINES FROM SEPARATE CIRCUITS COUPLED TOGETHER</li><li>OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER (ORC)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM PRE-DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>DETERMINE ACTIVE OR STORED DTC</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:            Make sure the battery is fully charged.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Perform the ORC module reset. Access the Miscellaneous Function menu from the ORC ECU Overview screen on the scan tool to perform this operation.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Using the scan tool, read ORC DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Is the DTC active or stored?</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">ORC - ACTIVE DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLE CODE (DTC)</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Go To 2</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">ORC - STORED DTC</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM INTERMITTENT TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK FOR ADDITIONAL ACTIVE SQUIB DTCS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Using the scan tool, read ORC DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Are there impact sensor specific DTCs set as active in addition to B0095-9A-RIGHT FRONTAL ACCELERATION SENSOR - COMPONENT OR SYSTEM OPERATING CONDITIONS?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair all other active impact sensor specific DTCs before repairing B0095-9A-RIGHT FRONTAL ACCELERATION SENSOR - COMPONENT OR SYSTEM OPERATING CONDITIONS.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>USE THE SCAN TOOL TO IDENTIFY THE COUPLED CIRCUITS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Using the scan tool, identify the two or more Impact Sensor circuits that read SET.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are two or more Impact Sensor circuits DTCs set?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the two or more impact sensor circuits for a Impact Sensor Circuit Coupling condition.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM INTERMITTENT TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b0099-96 roll over sensor component internal failure\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B0099-96</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">ROLL OVER SENSOR COMPONENT INTERNAL FAILURE</small><small>العطل: عطل داخلي بالمكوّن</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">When powered, the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) performs an internal self test. The repair of this fault condition does not involve any external circuitry and centers on verifying the integrity of the module&#x27;s roll over sensor.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">With the ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This DTC sets when the ORC detects corruption in the data and circuitry related to the internal roll over sensor. Once set, this DTC is latched for the entire ignition cycle. If the failure is detected in two consecutive power cycles, the DTC is set indefinitely.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This DTC may inhibit deployment or modify deployment strategy.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER (ORC)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM PRE-DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE OR STORED DTC</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:         Make sure the battery is fully charged.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read ORC DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Is the DTC active or stored?</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">ORC - ACTIVE DTC</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To2.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">ORC - STORED DTC</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM INTERMITTENT TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK RELATED HARNESS CONNECTIONS</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:      Turn the ignition off, disconnect the battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:      If the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) is dropped at any time, it must be replaced. Failure to take the proper precautions could result in accidental airbag deployment. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect all Occupant Restraint Controller(ORC) harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect all related in-line harness connections (if equipped).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Disconnect the related component harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Inspect harness connectors, component connectors, and all male and female terminals for the following conditions: Proper connector installation. Damaged connector locks. Corrosion. Other signs of water intrusion. Weather seal damage (if equipped). Bent terminals. Overheating due to a poor connection (terminal may be discolored due to excessive current</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">draw). Terminals that have been pushed back into the connector cavity. Check for spread terminals and verify proper terminal tension.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Repair any conditions that are found.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Connect all Occupant Restraint Controller(ORC) harness connectors. Be certain that all harness connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Connect all in-line harness connectors (if equipped). Be certain that all connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Connect all related component harness connectors. Be certain that all connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>Test drive or operate the vehicle in accordance with the when monitored and set conditions.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">10</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Replace and program the Occupant Restraint Controller in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, OCCUPANT RESTRAINT (ORC), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">The wiring or poor connection problem has been repaired.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the Occupant Restraint Controller VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b00b5-11 driver seat track position sensor circuit short to ground\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B00B5-11</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">DRIVER SEAT TRACK POSITION SENSOR CIRCUIT SHORT TO GROUND</small><small>العطل: قصر على الأرضي</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">When powered, the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) sends a test current to the seat track position sensors to verify the integrity of the sensors and wiring.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">With the ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">If the module detects a short to ground for a minimum of 2.5 seconds. This fault will go from active to stored status upon the short to ground fault clearing for 5 seconds.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This DTC may inhibit deployment or modify deployment strategy.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>DRIVER SEAT POSITION SENSOR DATA CIRCUIT SHORTED TO GROUND</li><li>DRIVER SEAT POSITION SENSOR VOLTAGE CIRCUIT SHORTED TO GROUND</li><li>DRIVER SEAT TRACK POSITION SENSOR</li><li>OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER (ORC)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM PRE-DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read ORC DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Record the Environmental Data.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using the recorded Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read ORC DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM INTERMITTENT TEST . Probing of the circuit cavities at the ORC Module body harness connectors or vehicle connectors is only to be done with a approved test lead from the test lead 10159-6 or the use of Breakout Box 8443-55 to prevent vehicle wiring harness connector damage during diagnostic procedures.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK FOR ACTIVE INTERNAL FAULTS, IGNITION FAULTS, AND BATTERY FAULTS IN THE OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER (ORC)</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read Occupant restraint Controller (ORC) DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the scan tool display any active DTCs relating to internal faults, ignition faults, or battery faults?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Diagnose and repair the DTCs. Refer to DIAGNOSTIC CODE INDEX .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>INSPECT DRIVER SEAT HARNESS WIRES AND CONNECTORS</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:      Turn the ignition off, disconnect the battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Using the wiring diagram/schematic as a guide, inspect the driver seat harness wiring and connectors. Look for chafed, pierced, pinched, or partially broken wires and broken, bent, pushed out, spread, corroded, or contaminated terminals.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Are any of these conditions present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Do not attempt to repair the Seat Harness. Replace the Seat Harness if the condition inspecting or testing for is present in the Seat Harness.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the driver seat harness in accordance with the Service Information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>VERIFY THAT DRIVER SEAT HARNESS IS ROUTED CORRECTLY</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Verify that the driver seat harness is routed correctly.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Is the Driver Seat Harness routed correctly?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 5</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Reroute the driver seat harness as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>CHECK (R261) DRIVER SEAT POSITION SENSOR DATA CIRCUIT AND (R263) DRIVER SEAT POSITION SENSOR VOLTAGE CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO GROUND</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Measure the resistance between ground and the (R261) Driver Seat Position Sensor Data circuit cavity 1.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Measure the resistance between ground and the (R263) Driver Seat Position Sensor Voltage circuit cavity 2.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance below 10k Ohms on either circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          Do not attempt to repair the Seat Harness. Replace the Seat Harness if the condition inspecting or testing for is present in the Seat Harness.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Driver Seat Harness in accordance with the service information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 6</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>CHECK (R261) DRIVER SEAT POSITION SENSOR DATA CIRCUIT AND (R263) DRIVER SEAT POSITION SENSOR VOLTAGE CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the ORC harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Connect the test leads to the DVOM.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (R261) Driver Seat Position Sensor Data circuit between the ORC module body harness connector cavity C2-83 and the Driver Seat Track Position Sensor connector cavity 1. 4.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (R263) Driver Seat Position Sensor Voltage circuit between the ORC module body harness connector cavity C2-84 and the Driver Seat Track Position Sensor connector cavity 2.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Is the resistance of either circuit above 5.0k Ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">نعم · Yes</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          Do not attempt to repair the Seat Harness. Replace the Seat Harness if the condition inspecting or testing for is present in the Seat Harness.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Replace the Driver Seat Harness in accordance with the Service Information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">لا · No</p><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:       Turn the ignition off, disconnect the battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:       If the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) is dropped at any time, it must be replaced. Failure to take the proper precautions can result in accidental airbag deployment.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Replace the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) in accordance with the service information. Refer to MODULE, OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b00b5-12 driver seat track position sensor circuit short to battery\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B00B5-12</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">DRIVER SEAT TRACK POSITION SENSOR CIRCUIT SHORT TO BATTERY</small><small>العطل: قصر على البطارية</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">When powered, the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) sends a test current to the seat track position sensors to verify the integrity of the sensors and wiring.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">With the ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">If the module detects that the sensor input is greater than 5K Ohms for a minimum of 2.5 seconds. This fault will go from active to stored status upon the short to battery fault clearing for 5 seconds.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This DTC may inhibit deployment or modify deployment strategy.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>DRIVER SEAT POSITION SENSOR DATA CIRCUIT SHORTED TO VOLTAGE</li><li>DRIVER SEAT POSITION SENSOR VOLTAGE CIRCUIT SHORTED TO VOLTAGE</li><li>DRIVER SEAT POSITION SENSOR DATA CIRCUIT SHORTED TO THE DRIVER SEAT POSITION</li><li>SENSOR VOLTAGE CIRCUIT</li><li>DRIVER SEAT TRACK POSITION SENSOR</li><li>OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER (ORC)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM PRE-DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read ORC DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Record the Environmental Data.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using the recorded Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read ORC DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM INTERMITTENT TEST . Probing of the circuit cavities at the ORC Module body harness connectors or vehicle connectors is only to be done with a approved test lead from the test lead 10159-6 or the use of Breakout Box 8443-55 to prevent vehicle wiring harness connector damage during diagnostic procedures.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK FOR ACTIVE INTERNAL FAULTS, IGNITION FAULTS, AND BATTERY FAULTS IN THE OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER (ORC)</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the scan tool display any active DTCs relating to internal faults, ignition faults, or battery faults?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Diagnose and repair the DTCs. Refer to DIAGNOSTIC CODE INDEX .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>INSPECT DRIVER SEAT HARNESS WIRES AND CONNECTORS</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:      Turn the ignition off, disconnect the battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Using the wiring diagram/schematic as a guide, inspect the passenger seat harness wiring and connectors. Look for chafed, pierced, pinched, or partially broken wires and broken, bent, pushed out, spread, corroded, or contaminated terminals.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Are any of these conditions present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Do not attempt to repair the Seat Harness. Replace the Seat Harness if the condition inspecting or testing for is present in the Seat Harness.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the driver seat harness in accordance with the Service Information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM INTERMITTENT TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>VERIFY THAT DRIVER SEAT HARNESS IS ROUTED CORRECTLY</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Verify that the driver seat harness is routed correctly.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Is the Driver Seat Harness routed correctly?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 5</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Reroute the driver seat harness as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>CHECK FOR DTC B00B5-12-DRIVER SEAT TRACK POSITION SENSOR - CIRCUIT SHORT TO BATTERY WITH DRIVER SEAT TRACK POSITION SENSOR DISCONNECTED</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:      Turn the ignition off disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">possible serious or fatal injury.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the Driver Seat Track Position Sensor connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the standard key ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:       Turn the ignition on, then reconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the keyless ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:       Disconnect the 12-volt battery wait two minutes before proceeding, remove the ORC fuses, connect the 12-volt battery, wait two minutes before proceeding. Cycle the ignition to the On position, then reconnect the ORC fuses. Wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Wait two minutes, and then with the scan tool, read ORC DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the scan tool display: B00B5-12-DRIVER SEAT TRACK POSITION SENSOR - CIRCUIT SHORT TO BATTERY?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 6</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:       Turn the ignition off, disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Driver Seat Track Position Sensor in accordance with the service information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Refer to SENSOR, SEAT TRACK POSITION, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>CHECK (R261) DRIVER SEAT POSITION SENSOR DATA CIRCUIT AND (R263) DRIVER SEAT POSITION SENSOR VOLTAGE CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO VOLTAGE</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:      Turn the ignition off, disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the ORC harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the standard key ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition on, then reconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the keyless ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Disconnect the 12-volt battery wait two minutes before proceeding, remove the ORC fuses, connect the 12-volt battery, wait two minutes before proceeding. Cycle the ignition to the On position, then reconnect the ORC fuses. Wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Measure the voltage of the (R261) Driver Seat Position Sensor Data circuit at the Driver Seat Track Position Sensor harness connector cavity 1.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Measure the voltage of the (R263) Driver Seat Position Sensor Voltage circuit at the Driver Seat Track Position Sensor harness connector cavity 2.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Is the voltage above 0.2 volt on either circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">نعم · Yes</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Do not attempt to repair the Seat Harness. Replace the Seat Harness if the condition inspecting or testing for is present in the Seat Harness.</div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition off, disconnect the battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Driver Seat Harness in accordance with the Service Information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 7</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>CHECK (R261) DRIVER SEAT POSITION SENSOR DATA CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO THE (R263) DRIVER SEAT POSITION SENSOR VOLTAGE CIRCUIT</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:       Turn the ignition off, disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Measure the resistance between the (R261) Driver Seat Position Sensor Data circuit cavity 1 and the (R263) Driver Seat Position Sensor Voltage circuit cavity 2 in the Passenger Seat Track Position Sensor harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Is the resistance below 10K Ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">نعم · Yes</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          Do not attempt to repair the Seat Harness. Replace the Seat Harness if the condition inspecting or testing for is present in the Seat Harness.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Replace the Driver Seat Harness in accordance with the service information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Replace the ORC in accordance with the Service information. Refer to MODULE, OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b00b5-13 driver track position sensor circuit open\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B00B5-13</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">DRIVER TRACK POSITION SENSOR CIRCUIT OPEN</small><small>العطل: دائرة مفتوحة</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">When powered, the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) sends a test current to the seat track position sensors to verify the integrity of the sensors and wiring.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">With the ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This Diagnostic Trouble Code (DTC) may set when the module detects that the sensor input current is below 1 mA. This fault will go from active to stored status upon the open fault clearing for 5 seconds.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This DTC may inhibit deployment or modify deployment strategy.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>DRIVER SEAT POSITION SENSOR DATA CIRCUIT OPEN</li><li>DRIVER SEAT POSITION SENSOR VOLTAGE CIRCUIT OPEN</li><li>DRIVER SEAT TRACK POSITION SENSOR</li><li>OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER (ORC) MODULE</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM PRE-DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read ORC DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Record the Environmental Data.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using the recorded Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read ORC DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM INTERMITTENT TEST . Probing of the circuit cavities at the ORC Module body harness connectors or vehicle connectors is only to be done with a approved test lead from the test lead 10159-6 or the use of Breakout Box 8443-55 to prevent vehicle wiring harness connector damage during diagnostic procedures.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>VERIFY THAT DTC B00B5-13-DRIVER TRACK POSITION SENSOR - CIRCUIT OPEN</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Does the scan tool display active B00B5-13-DRIVER TRACK POSITION SENSOR - CIRCUIT OPEN?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM INTERMITTENT TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>INSPECT DRIVER SEAT HARNESS WIRES AND CONNECTORS</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:       Turn the ignition off, disconnect the battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Using the wiring diagram/schematic as a guide, inspect the driver seat harness wiring and connectors. Look for chafed, pierced, pinched, or partially broken wires and broken, bent, pushed out, spread, corroded, or contaminated terminals.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Are any of these conditions present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Do not attempt to repair the passenger seat harness. Replace the passenger seat harness if any of these conditions exist.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the driver seat harness according to the Service Information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>VERIFY THE DRIVER SEAT HARNESS IS ROUTED CORRECTLY</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Verify the driver seat harness is routed correctly.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Is the driver seat harness routed correctly?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 5</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Reroute the driver seat harness as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>CHECK FOR DTC B00B5-13-DRIVER SEAT TRACK POSITION SENSOR - CIRCUIT OPEN WITH DRIVER SEAT TRACK POSITION SENSOR DISCONNECTED</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:       Turn the ignition off disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the Driver Seat Track Position Sensor harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the standard key ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition on, then reconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the keyless ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Disconnect the 12-volt battery wait two minutes before proceeding, remove the ORC fuses, connect the 12-volt battery, wait two minutes before proceeding. Cycle the ignition to the On position, then reconnect the ORC fuses. Wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Wait two minutes, then using a scan tool, read ORC DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the scan tool display: B00B5-13-DRIVER SEAT TRACK POSITION SENSOR - CIRCUIT OPEN?</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 6</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition off, disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the driver seat track position sensor according to the Service Information. Refer to SENSOR, SEAT TRACK POSITION, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>CHECK (R261) DRIVER SEAT POSITION SENSOR DATA CIRCUIT AND (R263) DRIVER SEAT POSITION SENSOR VOLTAGE CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO VOLTAGE</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:      Turn the ignition off, disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the ORC harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the standard key ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition on, then reconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the keyless ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Disconnect the 12-volt battery wait two minutes before proceeding, remove the ORC fuses, connect the 12-volt battery, wait two minutes before proceeding. Cycle the ignition to the On position, then reconnect the ORC fuses. Wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Measure the voltage of the (R261) driver seat position sensor data circuit between the driver seat track position sensor harness connector and ground.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Measure the voltage of the (R263) Driver Seat Position Sensor Voltage circuit between the driver seat track position harness connector and ground.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Is the voltage above 0.2 of a Volt for either circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">نعم · Yes</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Do not attempt to repair the driver seat harness. Replace the driver seat harness if any of these conditions exist.</div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        To avoid serious or fatal injury, turn the ignition off, disconnect the battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the driver seat harness according to the Service Information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 7</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>CHECK (R261) DRIVER SEAT POSITION SENSOR DATA CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO THE (R263) DRIVER SEAT POSITION SENSOR VOLTAGE CIRCUIT</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:      Turn the ignition off, disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Measure the resistance between the (R659) driver seat position sensor data circuit and the (R263) Driver Seat Position Sensor Voltage circuit in the Driver Seat Track Position Sensor harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Is the resistance below 10k Ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">نعم · Yes</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          Do not attempt to repair the seat harness. Replace the seat harness if any of these conditions exist.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Replace the driver seat harness according to the Service Information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Replace the ORC according to the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b00b5-2b driver seat track position sensor wires shorted together\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B00B5-2B</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">DRIVER SEAT TRACK POSITION SENSOR WIRES SHORTED TOGETHER</small><small>العطل: قصر بين الأسلاك</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">When powered, the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) sends a test current to the seat track position sensors to verify the integrity of the sensors and wiring.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">With the ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">If the module detects that the sensor input is greater than or equal to 17.1 mA. for minimum 2.5 seconds.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This DTC may inhibit deployment or modify deployment strategy.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>DRIVER SEAT HARNESS IMPROPERLY ROUTED</li><li>DRIVER SEAT HARNESS WIRES CHAFED, PIERCED, PINCHED, PARTIALLY BROKEN</li><li>DRIVER SEAT HARNESS CONNECTOR TERMINALS BROKEN, BENT, PUSHED OUT, SPREAD,</li><li>CORRODED, CONTAMINATED</li><li>DRIVER SEAT POSITION SENSOR DATA CIRCUIT</li><li>DRIVER SEAT POSITION SENSOR VOLTAGE CIRCUIT SHORTED</li><li>DRIVER SEAT POSITION SENSOR DATA CIRCUIT SHORTED TO DRIVER SEAT POSITION</li><li>SENSOR VOLTAGE CIRCUIT</li><li>DRIVER SEAT TRACK POSITION SENSOR</li><li>OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER (ORC)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM PRE-DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read ORC DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Record the Environmental Data.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using the recorded Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read ORC DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM INTERMITTENT TEST . Probing of the circuit cavities at the ORC Module body harness connectors or vehicle connectors is only to be done with a approved test lead from the test lead 10159-6 or the use of Breakout Box 8443-55 to prevent vehicle wiring harness connector damage during diagnostic procedures.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>VERIFY THAT DTC B00B5-2B-DRIVER SEAT TRACK POSITION SENSOR - WIRES SHORTED TOGETHER IS ACTIVE</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Does the scan tool display active: B00B5-2B-DRIVER SEAT TRACK POSITION SENSOR - WIRES SHORTED TOGETHER?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM INTERMITTENT TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>INSPECT DRIVER SEAT HARNESS WIRES AND CONNECTORS</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:         Turn the ignition off disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Using the wiring diagram/schematic as a guide, inspect the Driver Seat Harness wiring and connectors. Look for chafed, pierced, pinched, or partially broken wires and broken, bent, pushed out, spread, corroded, or contaminated terminals.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are any of these conditions present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Do not attempt to repair the Seat Harness. Replace the Seat Harness if any of these conditions exist</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Driver Seat Harness in accordance with the Service Information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>VERIFY THAT DRIVER SEAT HARNESS IS ROUTED CORRECTLY</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Verify that the Driver Seat Harness is routed correctly.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the Driver Seat Harness routed correctly?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 5</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Reroute the Driver Seat Harness as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>CHECK FOR DTC B00B5-2B-DRIVER SEAT TRACK POSITION SENSOR - WIRES SHORTED TOGETHER WITH DRIVER SEAT TRACK POSITION SENSOR DISCONNECTED</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:       Turn the ignition off disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the Driver Seat Track Position Sensor harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the standard key ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:       Turn the ignition on, then reconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the keyless ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:       Disconnect the 12-volt battery wait two minutes before proceeding, remove the ORC fuses, connect the 12-volt battery, wait two minutes before proceeding. Cycle the ignition to the On position, then reconnect the ORC fuses. Wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Wait two minutes, and then with the scan tool, read ORC DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the scan tool display: B00B5-2B-DRIVER SEAT TRACK POSITION SENSOR - WIRES SHORTED TOGETHER?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 6</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:       Turn the ignition off disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Replace the Driver Seat Track Position Sensor in accordance with the service information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Refer to SENSOR, SEAT TRACK POSITION, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>CHECK (R261) SEAT POSITION SENSOR DATA-DRIVER CIRCUIT AND (R263) SEAT POSITION SENSOR VOLTAGE-DRIVER CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO VOLTAGE</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:      Turn the ignition off disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the ORC harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the standard key ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition on, then reconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the keyless ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Disconnect the 12-volt battery wait two minutes before proceeding, remove the ORC fuses, connect the 12-volt battery, wait two minutes before proceeding. Cycle the ignition to the On position, then reconnect the ORC fuses. Wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Measure the voltage of the (R261) Driver Seat Position Sensor Data circuit between the Driver Seat Track Position Sensor harness connector and ground.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Measure the voltage of the (R263) Driver Seat Position Sensor Voltage circuit between the Driver Seat Track Position Sensor harness connector and ground.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Is the voltage above 0.2 volt on either circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">نعم · Yes</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          Do not attempt to repair the Seat Harness. Replace the Seat Harness if any of these conditions exist</div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:       Turn the ignition off disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Driver Seat Harness in accordance with the Service Information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 7</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>CHECK (R261) DRIVER SEAT POSITION SENSOR DATA CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO (R263) DRIVER SEAT POSITION SENSOR VOLTAGE CIRCUIT</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:      Turn the ignition off disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Measure the resistance between the (R261) Driver Seat Position Sensor Data circuit and the (R263) Driver Seat Position Sensor Voltage circuit in the Driver Seat Track Position Sensor harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Is the resistance below 10K Ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">نعم · Yes</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          Do not attempt to repair the Seat Harness. Replace the Seat Harness if any of these conditions exist</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Replace the Driver Seat Harness in accordance with the service information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Replace the ORC in accordance with the Service information. Refer to MODULE, OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b00b5-95 driver seat track position sensor incorrect assembly\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B00B5-95</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">DRIVER SEAT TRACK POSITION SENSOR INCORRECT ASSEMBLY</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">When powered, the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) sends a test current to the seat track position sensors. During this test, the sensors discovered are checked for agreement with the pre-programmed configuration of components assigned to the module.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The ORC checks for the presence of seat position sensor circuits once during the initialization process.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This DTC sets when the ORC detects the presence of a seat position sensor circuit while the configuration of the module does not reflect a seat track position sensor should be present. Once set, this DTC is latched for the entire power cycle and requires the module to be re-initalized to set code.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This DTC may inhibit deployment or modify deployment strategy.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>SEAT POSITION SENSORS</li><li>WIRING</li><li>OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER (ORC)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM PRE-DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read ORC DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Record the Environmental Data.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using the recorded Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read ORC DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM INTERMITTENT TEST . Probing of the circuit cavities at the ORC Module body harness connectors or vehicle connectors is only to be done with a approved test lead from the test lead 10159-6 or the use of Breakout Box 8443-55 to prevent vehicle wiring harness connector damage during diagnostic procedures.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>VERIFY THAT B00B5-95-DRIVER SEAT TRACK POSITION SENSOR - INCORRECT ASSEMBLY IS ACTIVE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, erase ORC DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Turn the ignition off, wait 10 seconds and then turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Wait 2 minutes, and then with the scan tool, read ORC DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the scan tool display active: B00B5-95-DRIVER SEAT TRACK POSITION SENSOR - INCORRECT ASSEMBLY?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>VERIFY WIRING</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Inspect the driver seat wiring for Seat Position Sensors.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Are Seat Position Sensor(s) present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:       Turn the ignition off, disconnect the battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:       If the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) is dropped at any time, it must be replaced. Failure to take the proper precautions can result in accidental airbag deployment.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the ORC in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b00b5-9a driver seat track position sensor component or system operating\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B00B5-9A</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">DRIVER SEAT TRACK POSITION SENSOR COMPONENT OR SYSTEM OPERATING</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">CONDITIONS</p></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">When powered, the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) sends a test current to the Seat Track Position sensor to verify the integrity of the sensor and wiring. The presence of this code indicates that any two circuits, from two or more sensors, have become shorted or &quot;coupled&quot; together.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The ORC checks the Seat Track Sensor circuits once during the initialization process.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Module detects that two Seat Track Sensor lines from separate circuits are coupled together.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Once set, the DTC is latched for the entire power cycle and requires the module to be re-initialized to transition code from active to stored. This DTC may inhibit deployment or modify deployment strategy.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>2 SEAT TRACK SENSOR LINES FROM SEPARATE CIRCUITS COUPLED TOGETHER</li><li>OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER (ORC)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM PRE-DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>DETERMINE ACTIVE OR STORED DTC</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          Make sure the battery is fully charged.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Perform ORC module reset. Access the Miscellaneous Function menu from the ORC ECU Overview screen on the scan tool to perform this operation.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Using the scan tool, read ORC DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Is the DTC active or stored?</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">ORC - ACTIVE DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLE CODE (DTC)</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">ORC - STORED DTC</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM INTERMITTENT TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK FOR ADDITIONAL ACTIVE SQUIB DTCS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Using the scan tool, read ORC DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Are there sensor specific DTCs set as active in addition to B0090-9A-LEFT FRONTAL RESTRAINTS SENSOR - COMPONENT OR SYSTEM OPERATING CONDITIONS?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair all other active sensor specific DTCs before repairing B0090-9A-LEFT FRONTAL RESTRAINTS SENSOR - COMPONENT OR SYSTEM OPERATING CONDITIONS.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>USE THE SCAN TOOL TO IDENTIFY THE COUPLED CIRCUITS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Using the scan tool, identify the two or more sensor circuits that read SET.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are two or more sensor circuits DTCs set?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the two or more sensor circuits for a Sensor Circuit Coupling condition.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM INTERMITTENT TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b1bc7-00 deployment data record full\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B1BC7-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">DEPLOYMENT DATA RECORD FULL</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">When powered, the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) performs an internal self test. The repair of this fault condition does not involve any external circuitry and centers on verifying the integrity of the module&#x27;s internal memory.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs once during the initialization process.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">With the ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This DTC sets when the ORC detects that five recorded deploy events have been reached. Once set, this DTC is latched indefinitely.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This DTC may inhibit deployment or modify deployment strategy.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER (ORC)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM PRE-DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">CHECK FOR ACTIVE DTC</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read ORC DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Is the Deployment Data Record Full DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        If the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) is dropped at any time, it must be replaced. Failure to take the proper precautions can result in accidental airbag deployment and serious or fatal injury.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the ORC in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b1bd3-00 non regular operation flag\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B1BD3-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">NON REGULAR OPERATION FLAG</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">NO TITLE</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">For a complete wiring diagram, refer to appropriate SYSTEM WIRING DIAGRAMS article .</p></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) is a sensing and diagnostic module that is responsible for monitoring and managing hard wired inputs, outputs, bussed messages and contains the vehicles Dynamics Sensor. The module contains the pre-programmed logic to determine if and when a restraint is to be deployed. The ORC monitors these systems at ignition on and for most systems, continuously during vehicle operation, communicating relevant status and data over the bus. If the ORC detects a system failure or monitored value that is out of the allowable range, a corresponding DTC will be set and recorded and the Airbag Warning lamp will be commanded on. In the event of a vehicle crash which exceeds a predetermined level, this may or may not include restraints deployment, crash data will be recorded and cannot be deleted. The Early Crash Sensors (Frontal Crash Sensors) are located on the front crossmember. The Remote Acceleration Sensors (B-Pillar Sensors) are located behind the trim of the B-Pillars. The Remote Acceleration Sensors (C-Pillar Sensors) are located behind the trim of the C-Pillars. The Door Pressure Sensors (if equipped) are located in the front doors and the Yaw and Lateral Sensors are internal to the controller.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">With the ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This DTC sets when the ORC detects a Rollover Sensor internal failure condition.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This DTC may or may not inhibit deployment or modify deployment strategy.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER (ORC)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM PRE-DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read ORC DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC still active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>REPLACE THE OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER (ORC)</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition off disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        If the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) is dropped at any time, it must be replaced. Failure to take the proper precautions could result in accidental airbag deployment. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">When this code is set, view repair.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Repair</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Replace the ORC in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b212c-13 ignition run/start input-circuit open\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B212C-13</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">IGNITION RUN/START INPUT-CIRCUIT OPEN</small><small>العطل: دائرة مفتوحة</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) Module receives power from both a battery and ignition feed input circuits from the Power Distribution Center. These circuits power the ORC Module and the capacitors used to initiate the squib deployment circuits in the event of collision detection.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">With the ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This Diagnostic Trouble Code (DTC) sets when the ORC Module fails to detect ignition voltage or if there is less than 6 volts on the ignition voltage supply circuit for more than 15 seconds while the battery circuit maintains system operating voltage. In the event the ORC Module detects voltage has returned to normal operating range for a minimum of five seconds, this DTC immediately transitions to stored status.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This DTC may inhibit deployment or modify deployment strategy.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>ACTIVE POWER DISTRIBUTION CENTER TROUBLE CODES</li><li>RUN/START RELAY CIRCUIT OPEN</li><li>RUN/START FUSE OPEN</li><li>FUSED RUN/START RELAY OUTPUT CIRCUIT OPEN OR SHORTED TO GROUND</li><li>OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER (ORC)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM PRE-DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read ORC DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Record the Environmental Data.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using the recorded Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read ORC DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM INTERMITTENT TEST . Probing of the circuit cavities at the ORC Module body harness connectors or vehicle connectors is only to be done with a approved test lead from the test lead 10159-6 or the use of Breakout Box 8443-55 to prevent vehicle wiring harness connector damage during diagnostic procedures.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>INSPECT AIRBAG RUN-START FUSE F65</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Remove and inspect fuse F65 from the Power Distribution Center (PDC).</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          Check connectors. Clean and repair as necessary.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is fuse F65 open?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Go To 4</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK (F201) FUSED IGNITION SWITCH OUTPUT (RUN-START) CIRCUIT RESISTANCE</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:       Turn the ignition off then disconnect the battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious and fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (F201) Fused Run Start Relay Output (Run-Start) circuit between ground and fuse F65 terminal (output side).</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance below 100.0 Ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Using the wiring diagram/schematic as a guide, inspect the related wiring and connectors. Look for chafed, pierced, pinched, or partially broken wires and broken, bent, pushed out, spread, corroded, or contaminated terminals.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Replace fuse F65.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK (F201) FUSED IGNITION SWITCH OUTPUT (RUN-START) CIRCUIT RESISTANCE WITH ORC CONNECTORS DISCONNECTED</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:       If the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) is dropped at any time, it must be replaced. Failure to take the proper precautions could result in accidental airbag deployment. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:       Turn the ignition off disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect both ORC harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Check connectors - Clean and repair as necessary.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Connect the appropriate test lead to the DVOM.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (F201) Fused Ignition Switch Output (Run-Start) circuit between the appropriate terminals of the ORC module body harness connector and ground.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance below 100.0 Ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 5</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:         If the Occupant Restraint Controller is dropped at any time, it must be replaced. Failure to take the proper precautions can result in accidental airbag deployment and serious or fatal injury.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the ORC in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Airbag Run-Start Fuse F65.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>CHECK (F201) IGNITION SWITCH OUTPUT (RUN-START) CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the standard key ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:         Turn the ignition on, then reconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the keyless ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:         Disconnect the 12-volt battery wait two minutes before proceeding, remove the ORC fuses, connect the 12-volt battery, wait two minutes before proceeding. Cycle the ignition to the On position, then reconnect the ORC fuses. Wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Measure the voltage of the (F201) Ignition Switch Output (Run-Start) circuit at the Airbag Run- Start fuse F65 terminal (supply side).</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the voltage above 6.0 volts?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Go To 6</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:         Turn the ignition off disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Repair the open (F201) Ignition Switch Output (Run-Start) circuit.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>CHECK (F201) FUSED IGNITION SWITCH OUTPUT (RUN-START) CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN</span></div><pre class=\"en-pre\">          WARNING:         Turn the ignition off, disconnect the battery and wait two minutes\n                           before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in\n     1.                    possible serious or fatal injury.</pre><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Reinstall the Airbag Run-Start Fuse F65.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Disconnect both ORC harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Check connectors - Clean and repair as necessary.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Install the appropriate test lead to the DVOM.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the standard key ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition on, then reconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the keyless ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Disconnect the 12-volt battery wait two minutes before proceeding, remove the ORC fuses, connect the 12-volt battery, wait two minutes before proceeding. Cycle the ignition to the On position, then reconnect the ORC fuses. Wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Measure the voltage of the (F201) Fused Ignition Switch Output (Run-Start) Circuit between the appropriate terminals of the ORC module body harness connector and ground.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the voltage above 6.0 volts?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 7</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the open (F201) Fused Ignition Switch Output (Run-Start) circuit.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>VERIFY THAT DTC B212C-13-IGNITION RUN/START INPUT CIRCUIT OPEN DTC IS ACTIVE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Reconnect both ORC harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the standard key ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition on, then reconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the keyless ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Disconnect the 12-volt battery wait two minutes before proceeding, remove the ORC fuses, connect the 12-volt battery, wait two minutes before proceeding. Cycle the ignition to the On position, then reconnect the ORC fuses. Wait two minutes before proceeding.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>With the scan tool, read ORC DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Select the module displaying the active: B212C-13-IGNITION RUN/START INPUT - CIRCUIT OPEN?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">نعم · Yes</p><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:       If the Occupant Restraint Controller (ORC) is dropped at any time, it must be replaced. Failure to take the proper precautions could result in accidental airbag deployment. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:       Turn the ignition off, disconnect the battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Replace the ORC in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Article GUID: A00910369</p></div></div></details></div></details></div>";
